!! The loops ~ the strides that hold every open row

No row rests here: each sits in the stride below that holds it, and a citation names that stride. Each row names what stays owed, the train of #/the-trains that closes it, and who owes a ruling first
(''operator'', ''house'', or nobody). A row names its file so a builder reads the code before leaning on
the row; a line number drifts, so none rests here. Train letters: ''L'' the memory-stage hearth ·
''T'' the test re-cut · ''S'' the custody seal · ''G'' ground ·
''K'' the seat · ''N'' the Nexus founding act · ''P'' the Kahu plane · ''W'' the wire and the face proof ·
''E'' the ember · ''O1'' ONE FACE's sessions · ''H'' the hosted road ·
''A'' HARBOR's tail · ''V'' recovery's verbs · ''B'' the browser and the phones · ''X'' TWO HEARTHS · ''R'' block and inline sigils at parsing parity (one lane, no rows; its R-prefixed namesakes, R-CHARTER and its kin, name the re-found's stages).
DreamDOM's train ''D'' keeps its rows in its own roadmap (#/side-lanes).

* ''#/stride-0-hearth'' — the memory-stage hearth: the joined walk, the stage, the seat.
* ''#/stride-t-recut'' — the test re-cut: wave 0's cures, then waves A to C.
* ''#/stride-1-spine'' — face and custody; sealed identity and private authority.
* ''#/stride-2-floor'' — floor, wire and realm release.
* ''#/stride-3-bake'' — one re-bake, rename and founding format.
* ''#/after-the-seat'' — remaining work and witnesses.
* ''#/operator-gates'' — operator rulings and hands.
* ''#/o-takiage'' — complete rows moved by the rite.

