<<~ ahu slot=`#/stride-0-hearth`>>

!! Stride 0 Hearth

The memory-stage hearth (#/the-attractor; #/rulings, 2026-10-31): the joined walk first, then the stage on it, then the move. Each row runs red-first with its control; a row's harness half walks the test door, and the operator's hand performs each founding and custody act (#/cold-start).

!!! Seven-league stride notes

* ''MEASURED, the walk as it stands'' (the hearth walk and the pronaos read, 2026-10-31, on a scratch root): each of the rite's thirteen steps stands in code (stage, build, found, stand, unlock, seed, the page, the browser floor, the slot, the offer, the request, the answer, the land and its settle); a CLI `meme get` and `meme put` against a bag work; the daemon's own port answers 404 at `/`, so the page arrives only from a separate Vite server, faceless and unjoined; a page edit's arrival on disk stands unmeasured; the MCP seat fails before it speaks.
* ''The stage's design, a house lean the controller rules through `L8`'' (the stage scout, two rounds, 2026-10-31): tags and one index view on the daemon wiki; a working stage in a named wiki git leaves untracked, its loss cheap by design; an episodic tier in one thin checked-in named wiki a cold clone needs; survivors reaching `bags/` carriers by promotion; `stage/*` standing beside `lifecycle/*` as a sibling family, so an unpoured row never enters the governed count and a row poured as a carrier takes `lifecycle/*` at the pour; consolidation through a sitting, and through a talk-story floor where a row contradicts held canon; no row reads a clock.
* ''Where the operator's hearth stands'': the house as a container puts all code in the image (#/rulings). `L1`'s first move measures whether `tools/lares-container.sh up` already serves the page and where its projection writes; the cure derives the page's inputs once, for the container entry and for `lares vessel stand` alike, so a scratch walk and the operator's hearth read one composition.
* ''The operator's hand on the hearth'', each when its row stands: move the old homes aside and found fresh by hand (#/fresh-start; #/rulings, 2026-10-31, a single operator's re-found); unlock; bind the browser's passphrase slot; carry the fleet-join offer, request, answer and land; run `lares home tend` from the main clone, now that `L3` landed (PR #148). None of these gates a lane.

!!! The rows

* `L1` The stand serves the page: its tail. `lares vessel stand --page` serves the built page from the bare stand and declares same origin only where none stands declared (PR #143). Owed: each of `--restart`, `--foreground` and `--with-web` carries the page or refuses by name, where today `--page` drops under them with a warning alone. Red: `stand --page --restart` on a staged scratch root answers 200 `text/html` at `/`, or refuses naming the mode; control: a bare `stand --page` serves as it does today. L.
* `L2` The page dials its own origin: its tail. A node-served page dials its own origin's relay once `/.well-known/lar` answers as a Lararium (PR #143). Owed: a same-origin probe that stalls holds the page's boot with no way out; a person's act, a "boot local" control, ends the wait, never a timer (#/rulings, no global now). Red: a stalled `/.well-known/lar` with the control pressed boots local; control: an answering probe dials its origin as today. A shore lane. L.
* `L4` The stage walk (walk gap G3), carrying `FW`'s middle (`W5` and `W7`). A joined browser edits a tiddler in the daemon wiki, the file lands at `<LAR_ROOT>/wikis/daemon/`, and `lares meme get --recipe default` returns it; a CLI `meme put` shows in the page; the MCP seat reads the page's edit. Red: that walk on `tools/browser-weld/`, the join stepped through the test door; weakening control: with the relay killed, no file lands. It reads rung 2 whole (#/the-road, the shore). Waits on `L1`, `L2` and `L3`; where the daemon wiki's working layer needs a session signer, it waits on `U1` too, and the red names which. L; B.
* `F11` The hands: the watcher as a leasing session, the seat under a standing grant, the Mask as a record field, door parity at the session (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract#/the-hands`>>). An agent's dissent drafts and a person's direct ask edits (#/rulings, 2026-10-16). O1. The hand-profile gate stays owed here: `session:call` and `session:act` check the face and the anchor, never the hand, so a watcher's or a tab's session runs a face row as its face until the profile-verb table lands. Pulled forward to the hearth (2026-10-31): before any agent writes the operator's own hearth, an MCP seat's session calling a vault, admit or face-switch verb refuses by profile, and its `meme_put` carries its Mask; the watcher's lease and door parity land in the same row behind them.
* `L6` The seed reads two of six on a fresh root (measured three times on `440abf0f0`): each of the four user wikis refuses its `LOAD` with `bag not registered: lar:///ha.ka.ba/wikis/<slug>/working` (`keyhive-provider.ts`), while the Kahu canon converges; the founding walk of PR #128 read six of six. First move: one measure on `bf8461c4d` against `440abf0f0`, naming a regression since #128 or the known per-title seed-grain fault; then the cure, red-first. The hearth seeds the daemon wiki's neighbours, so it ranks with the walk. L.
* `L7` A command beside a standing vessel waits (the hearth walk): `lares persona new` while a vessel stands answers "store door is still held" and waits, where the one-store-door law sends it through the standing vessel or refuses it by name (#/decisions, one store door). Red: stand, run `persona new`, and the act lands through the vessel's door or refuses naming the door, never a wait; control: with no vessel standing, it owns the store. L.
* `L8` The memory-stage carrier: `docs/pono/memory-stage` holds the stage as law. The stage lives in the `daemon` wiki itself (operator ruling, 2026-10-31, #/rulings): its working layer projects to `<LAR_ROOT>/wikis/daemon/`, and no other wiki domain hosts it, since each serves its own intent. The carrier rules the tiers as tags inside that one wiki, the `stage/*` family beside `lifecycle/*`, what of the daemon wiki git keeps (`git ls-files wikis` reads none today) and how a survivor promotes into a bag carrier, the consolidation rite, the cold-boot index, and the rhymes with the field (complementary learning systems, hippocampal indexing, reconsolidation, the agent-memory systems), each with its source and where it breaks. Its first commit carries canon. L.
* `L9` Stage rows key by their content: each stage tiddler's title and id derive from its row key (the event, the row letter, the commit), never a clock or a counter, so a re-pour after a re-found reproduces the same tiddlers (#/rulings, 2026-10-31, a single operator's re-found). Red: pour one stage export onto two freshly founded roots, and titles and bodies match; control: a changed row key yields a new title. L.
* `L10` The lifecycle tools read the stage: `meme check` counts no `stage/*` row among governed carriers, and `lares meme sitting` names closed stage rows with a landed witness as burn candidates and burns none (`carrier-lifecycle.ts`). Red: a `stage/working` row with no witness passes `meme check`, and a closed row with a witness appears in the sitting; control: a `lifecycle/designed` carrier still meets its gate. L.
* `L11` The cold-boot index: one filter view on the daemon wiki lists the open stage rows, each beside the commit or wave that last re-checked it and an `unchecked` mark where none did, and the boot set stays one fixed small read whatever the history holds. Red: a row whose named file moved since its last check reads `unchecked`; control: a re-checked row reads its stamp. L.
* `L12` The recurrence loop: an incident row carries `recurs/N`, counted by repeat incidents, never a clock; at two a sitting proposes a procedural change (a feedback line or a guard test, red-first), the operator rules it, and a lesson stays `unverified` until a later incident shows it held, a lesson that never fires reading as a burn candidate. Red: a second incident of one tell raises the proposal; control: one incident raises none. L.
* `L13` The move, the rung's acceptance: the controller's plan, its owed list, the scout reports, the lane briefs, the resume sheets and the record patches move onto the stage, and each scratch file burns by otakiage once its rows stand there; a cold session reads the stage index, this carrier and the controller handoff (#/cold-start). The harness's own auto-memory keeps its seat, since its host loads it through its own door; the reality tunnel's memory shore may later point it at the stage (#/side-lanes). Its witness: one cold session resumes the controller's work from the stage alone. L.
* `L14` The promotion verb, landing last: `meme promote` holds no in-wiki path, its admin check answers `false` (`meme.ts`), and the hand-edit weld stays unbuilt (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/wiki-layer-ontology`>>). Red: a person holding admin promotes a working-layer meme into a bag as a residency move, its `lar:` URI unchanged; control: a seat's promotion refuses. Until it lands, a stage row reaches `bags/` as a carrier poured by pull request. L.
* `L15` A live house beside the land train: with the operator's house mounted on the dev checkout, its projection dirties tracked `bags/` files, and a dirty tracked file blocks the land train's fast-forward on that path. Owed: the house's projection writes commit as their own record commits (or the train reads and carries them) before a land, and the tree-clean witness reads the house surface apart from a test boot's writes. Red: a standing house edits a canon tiddler, a train lands a commit touching another file, and the land succeeds with the house edit kept. L.
* `L16` The non-dev install: `LARES_WORKSPACE` names a corpus directory with no repository (seeded from the image's genesis and release bags), and `tools/lares-container.sh` stands the house on it unchanged. Red: a scratch corpus dir with no `.git` founds, stands and projects. L.
* `L17` The MCP seat carries the whole TiddlyWiki surface on any loaded wiki (operator, 2026-10-31: //"The MCP server should also have full TW5 caps on any wiki loaded."//): for each wiki the island runs, the seat reads and writes tiddlers with their fields, runs a filter and returns titles or fields, renders a tiddler or a wikitext span through the engine (wikify to text or HTML), lists shadows and plugins, and dispatches an action string or `tm-*` message, each through the island's own engine, never a second parser, and the CLI answers the same verbs (`lares meme filter|render|act ...`, MCP `meme_filter`, `meme_render`, `meme_act`, the `meme_put`/`meme_get` field forms). Capability, never host, bounds it: an action reaches only the verbs a page's session reaches under the same face (custody verbs keep their confirm door and face gate, `F11`'s seat profile holds the hand), and a write lands on the wiki's working layer (wikis-first). Today `meme_list` lists and nothing filters, renders or acts. Red: a tag filter over a seeded daemon wiki answers its titles; a render of a transcluding tiddler answers its text; an action string that sets a field lands it; controls: a malformed filter refuses by name, and an action naming a custody verb refuses without the face's confirm. L.
* `L18` The narration fence: self-narration, design notes, talk-story floors and their moʻolelo and hoike, scout reports, lane briefs, resume sheets, and the controller's plan and owed rows land in the daemon wiki through `meme_put`, never as files on disk. The fence rides three hands: the lead law and `mixed-model-swarm` carry the rule; a harness hook refuses a write to the controller's scratch notes and to the flat memory store beyond its pointer file, naming `meme_put` (installed through the operator's own config act); a witness counts stray narration files. Red: an agent's write to the fenced path refuses and names the wiki verb; control: a lane's code edit in its worktree passes. Lands after `L13`. L.
* `L19` The memory o-takiage: the flat memory store moves into the daemon wiki, each file a tiddler keyed by its slug (`stage/feedback`, `stage/semantic`, `stage/reference`, the `[[name]]` links kept as wiki links), checked against the repo as it moves (a memory that names a file, function or flag gets re-verified, and a stale one burns rather than moves); each moved file burns from the flat store; the index file shrinks to a pointer whose first line names the MCP capabilities and the cold-boot filter. Red: a cold session reads a moved memory through `meme_get` and the filter view, with the flat file gone; control: the pointer's first line answers before any wiki stands. Lands after `L18`. L.
* `L20` The fiction and art domains' o-takiage (#/rulings, 2026-11-01). Once the lararium stands, the RPG chapters and the concept art take wiki domains of their own under `edition/*` and `art/*` tag families, each with an o-takiage rite fitted to it and designed from the pono sweep; the domain sweep of 2026-11-01 found no RPG or art wiki yet, and lifecycle tags already read opt-in. The lares design laws never bind these families by default. Red: a carrier tagged `edition/*` passes `meme check` under its own family's law and meets no `lifecycle/*` gate it never opted into; control: a `lifecycle/designed` carrier in `bags/lares` still meets its gate. Waits on `L13`. L.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/stride-t-recut`>>

!! Stride T Recut

The test re-cut (#/rulings, 2026-10-31; #/the-road, train T; kit <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/test-recut-road`>>). Wave 0 ranks right behind the hearth (#/the-order); waves A and B follow as slots free; wave C waits on its gates. No lane opens on a cut row until its cold read and its collision read stand (#/rulings, 2026-10-31). A complete row moves to #/o-takiage at its land.

!!! Seven-league stride notes

* ''Landed, wave 0'': lane `recut-gates` landed `T19`, `T22` and `T27` (PR #141), the sweep's owner standing as a transport-free mesh stage (`gateSweep`) that `T13` inherits; `recut-custody` landed `T20` (PR #138); `recut-rolls` landed `T33` to `T35` (PR #144). Each moved to #/o-takiage, and each tail stands as a porch row (#/side-lanes).
* ''Beside the train'': `testlever` landed the test levers (PR #139), `ci-ten` the ten-job CI (PR #145), `land-queue` the local merge queue (PR #146), and `kdf-native` the native passphrase KDF with the lazy keyslot open (PR #147), which opens `T37`; the cells and shards rebalance keeps its tail (#/side-lanes).
* ''After Q'': ''Q'' landed (PR #149), so `T2`'s package codemod and the founded-custody template (`T36`) open; the canon-law lane (`T38`) waits on ''R'' too, so `meme check` takes one re-cut (#/the-order).

!!! Wave 0 ~ the cures the cut reads found, ahead of any cut

Each row here stands confirmed by two readers from source; each row's first commit runs its red, and a red that stays green retires the row or its clause.

* `T21` ''Cabal invites run more than once'' (security). `cabalInviteId` names a seen-cache that no code builds; only the epoch lease expires an invite, so a removed joiner re-presents it until the epoch advances. The law stands: a removed joiner never re-enters on an invite minted before the removal; the red decides the mechanism (#/the-floor). Red: remove a joiner, re-present the invite inside the same epoch, assert refusal. The next wave-0 slot.
* `T23` ''An admitted browser leaf bricks on reload'' (correctness, fails closed). The admit bootstrap keeps the hearth gate key but drops the island kind and scope; later boots pass a null anchor, the island falls to the leaf's own key, and the Binding Gate throws "chain absent". A same-tab reboot hides it; a reload exposes it; it bites when the gate key stands. Node cures the same case by re-reading its pin each boot. Red: admit, then boot again with no admit, assert the same island key; controls: a null-gate admit, a founded leaf. The cure reads no old bootstrap shape.
* `T24` ''The browser catalog orphans wikis'' (correctness). After a data-amnesia re-found the browser never rewrites its catalog pointer, so every later boot re-founds a blank catalog and orphans the wikis registered since; the first boot also writes the pointer before a store flush. Red: boot twice on a missing catalog document, assert the second boot stays quiet; cure includes a flush before the boot keys write.
* `T25` ''A failed wiki-switch flips the browser surface''. The browser handler tests the result object, always truthy, where node reads `.ok`. `T13`'s shared switcher cures it; the red lands first.
* `T26` ''A herm registers wiki verbs it cannot run''. They throw a TypeError on use (the CLI shore reaches `wiki-act`); the wiki verbs register behind the wiki capability.
* `T28` ''Wax-stamp verification owes its test''. `verifyWaxStampSig` and `mintWaxStamp` stand with no caller and fail closed; the test rides `W30`.
* `T29` ''Unborn seats state their law''. `peerContractNymMap` (the realm consult's root map, `membership-doctrine#/two-maps`) and `walkerBoard` (the reader half of the owed E walker arm) read as unborn seats, never dead code: their comments restate as law and name their owed rows. A seat with no road row and no canon behind it burns.
* `T37` ''The keyslot's key hygiene'' (custody, security read). Landed ahead in PR #147 (lane `kdf-native`): the passphrase KDF rides a minted port at one cost (native scrypt on the host, noble in the browser, identical bytes); a pin derives a passphrase only when it tries it and stops at the first share, so a right first guess pays one derivation where it paid three; each distinct passphrase counts as one attempt, charged before the open and refunded only on an open or a reading that ran no derivation; a face founding derives before its index entry lands; a KDF refusal zeroes the keys the unlock already opened. Owed, each red-first with its control: the keyslot never zeroes its scrypt material, KEK, slot key or shares (`keyslot.ts`); `doUnlock` leaks the tree key and secret key, and `doUnlockFace` the face key, when the root carrier's open throws, and the CLI's proof leaves its tree key unzeroed; a route keys on encoded bytes, or refuses a passphrase `isWellFormed` rejects, since lone surrogates collapse today; the door types `kdf-refused` as its refusal reason, where it reads `act-failed`; the window where a face's index entry stands before its key stores stays narrowed, never closed. The lazy open's timing reads as a MEDIUM oracle the day any remote unlock or proof door stands. S.

!!! Wave A ~ parallel, none touches the composer

* `T2` The shared scratch fixture: its codemod. The fixture (`tests/support/scratch-fixture.ts`) sets and restores `HOME`, `LAR_ROOT` and `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL` and refuses a leak by name; its pilot took 19 node suites (PR #142). Owed: the codemod by package, open now that ''Q'' landed. Red-first per package: a test that leaks its env reads red; the fixture twin stays green.
* `T4` The dead-export sweep, regenerated by a whole-tree token index: 67 names occur once in the tree. 35 burn; 12 carry a value another file re-spells inline, and those get imported where they belong rather than deleted (the node carrier-name regexes `vault-carriers.ts` re-spells); 14 wait on rulings; 6 stand (`serveHostingMint` for train H, the two `SIBLING_*_KIND` constants, the two `session-contract` compile-time witnesses, `TW5SyncAdaptor`). About 25 of the mesh names ride `export *` or a package subpath, so the sweep changes the published surface of `@lararium/mesh`. Red-first: the typecheck witness and `tools/evergreen-boundary.mjs` must bite on a deleted name that keeps a consumer before their zero counts. Lands as one announced batch right after a controller land. The 487 barrel names wait on their own ruling.
* `T5` The pure readers out of the composer: the torn-face check (after `ralias`), `diskMirrorGrant`, the pure parts of `postureOf`, `contractHolds` and `gateNexuses` (with a case-fold row for the dedup), the three cloned `askIslandMemory` getters collapsing to one (the getter shells stay, reading the atom lazily), and the wiki-act router. The router and its twin `routedWikiSlug` (`lararium-tw5/src/verb-local-dispatch.ts`) agree except on an explicit `wiki:"daemon"` and the no-slug fallback, so they become one pure function with the daemon passthrough as a named parameter, proven by a seed table against both callers. The bootstrap parse leaves this row: `ralias` replaces it with `readBootTiddlers`. Three source-regex witnesses retarget in the same commit as a cut: `faced-boot-requires-proof.test.ts`, `kahu-canon-wiring.test.ts` (three patterns) and `tools/seed-census.mjs`. The `daemonAuth` builder lands as one pure shared builder in mesh with a sentinel-seed no-leak test (it carries a seed for every unlocked joined face), and the boot pin list unifies across node and browser (#/the-floor).
* `T36` ''The founded-custody template'' (the fixture's probe, 2026-11-01). Each run founds real custody about 600 times at about 1.2 s each, and that founding holds the node suite's wall. Owed: ONE real `foundCustody` per run per standard route (`fixture-custody-passphrase`, 388 foundings in 54 files; `test-founding-passphrase`, 177 in 37), copied elsewhere, opt-in per file, every unlock still paying real scrypt; it serves about 309 foundings in 59 files, about 90 to 125 s of a node suite near 1200 s, while 34 files keep fresh foundings (founding, restore, rotation, keys, two vaults). Hazard: copies carry identical key bytes, so no two-vessel test takes one. Red: a templated file opens a copy under its own route and reads its own writes; control: a two-vessel test refuses the template by name. Open now that ''Q'' landed.
* `T38` ''The canon-law lane''. `status-why` and the shape laws a canon-reading test enforces move into `meme check` and the commit hook, scoped by domain (a tag family, a path class, or universal), and a CI canon cell runs them on a meme-only head, which `paths-ignore` skips today and which `ci.yml` offers no `workflow_dispatch` to raise. Red: a staged governed carrier with no `status-why` refuses at the hook and in the cell; control: a governed carrier carrying one passes. Follows ''R''.

!!! Wave B ~ beside the road, after T2 and T3

* `T6` Boot characterization: pins the stage order, port contracts and teardown-on-refuse of both vessels' boots, test-only. Its first red records the cap build order through an injected list and asserts `systemCanon` (inside the substrate cap) fires before the daemon cap's first gate, dial or sibling channel: no test pins that order today, and reordering the cap list or adding an extra cap with no `requires` breaks nothing. `systemCanon` becomes required in the keel type, so the compiler holds the share verdict's order too. Each pin lands with a mutant that breaks the order and must go red. The compose-hunk owner updates a pin in the same commit. `T12` waits on it.
* `T7` Events for the remaining flake families: the TW5 dropdown's ready signal plus failure artifacts, the browser two-tab unlock event, the staged unlock waiting on the store's acknowledgement (that last item routes through the compose-hunk owner). Red-first per item: a late event reds the fixed wait; a never-event control fails loudly, naming the missing edge. It carries `G46`'s load flakes whole: the custody census's staged unlock, the mesh scale ratio (`sensorium-consistency.scale.test.ts`, a wall-clock ratio a count of operations replaces) and the `shore-writes` dropdown case, each red reproducing its flake by the product's own event, never by load; the six `lararium-node` suites that read the operator's global git email took a hermetic `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL` in porch bundle five (PR #137), and `T20` retires the email from custody.
* `T8` The test-only export census, built by the compiler; the moves ride whichever lane cuts each module.
* `T30` The layer map: what each test layer proves (unit, island, vessel, mesh, held-out), what runs on every push and what runs on a batch, and where a slow witness waits on an event it means rather than a turn count, written into the kit before wave C cuts. Its inputs beside `T7`: fixed waits become events (`setImmediate` turn loops and fixed `setTimeout` ordering waits, `owned-store` first). Red-first per moved wait, as `T7` reads.
* `T31` The tw5 corpus scans share one measured budget in the vitest config, measured before it binds. Red: a scan past the budget reads red by name; control: the measured corpus passes.
* `T32` Node's slowest test files get profiled from the per-file durations CI records, and the profile names the first cuts for `T2` and `T9` to take.

!!! Wave C ~ the seams and the cut

* `T9` Instance-owned doors: one `VesselDoors` record handed to each worker handle, retiring the five process globals of `worker-handle.ts` (the rest, cas, dyad and custody-write doors, and the session sign door `U1` added in PR #140) with no ambient fallback; `tools/capability-inventory.mjs` changes in the same commit (it sets the first four and names an `answerBrowserDyadAsk` that exists nowhere). Red-first: two handles in one process answer distinct asks; the stale cas door a refused boot left fell to `T27` (PR #141). The row's scope stops at the doors. Two vessels per process stay unlawful after this row alone: custody `seats`, `mountedFace`, the Kahu classification writes, hosting-carry, the switch-act log, face-route and the env `LAR_ROOT` live process-wide too, and each names its own owner before any composition shares a process.
* `T10` Boot cells, in two kinds: seven cells refuse a read before set by name (`vmManager`, `wikiActivation`, `mailbox`, `daemonVm`, `eventBus`, `bootstrap`, `pendingVerbContribution`; today `sync-wiki` and `wiki-act` throw a bare TypeError before the pool stands), and the share-verdict inputs keep a typed closed default and ride with `T11`. Waits on `T6`, `u1` and `ralias`.
* `T11` Share inputs: one cell feeds the already-pure `selfSlotShareDecision`, which moves to mesh as the peer share verdict, tested as a decision table that keeps every fail-closed branch wave one walked. Each null input withholds by name rather than allowing (`T22`). Two share verdicts stand today (the browser runs `federationShareDecision`); the lane reads both first and lands one law per relation (#/the-floor). Waits on `ralias`.
* `T12` The stage-cut: the composer splits into the cap-stack stages and the orchestration record, behind capability-named ports, landing whole with no second shape. `openDaemon` fuses four jobs (face and custody resolve, board stand and climb, dial and register, daemon open with its verb providers), and its phase order and fail-closed throws survive the split: pure deciders come out first, then stages after `T6`. The custody half never becomes a stage a surface reaches. One named single-owner road step; every other lane stops at module boundaries for its window.
* `T13` Shared cap-stack stages: one stage per PR into mesh or tw5, the browser twin burning in the same PR. Ready: dyads, the sibling channel, the climb call, the offering-lookup half of the pool wiring, the switcher verbs, the after-daemon pins once `ralias` lands. Converging on node's fuller form (#/the-floor): the fleet shadow read, face proof and plane registration, island resolution (with `T23`'s cure), founding and admit, and the persona, face and circle verbs (a lift that grows node's verbs, not a collapse). Stand apart by design: the catalog, wiki-sense and the pools. The gate sweep already stands shared (`gateSweep`, PR #141). A stage that reads one of the process-wide states `T9` names (custody `seats`, `mountedFace`, the Kahu classification writes, hosting-carry, the switch-act log, face-route, the env `LAR_ROOT`) takes it through its port, never the global. The net collapse reads 200 to 400 lines.
* `T14` The verb math: a plain pure module first (its `coupleMesh` and `crystallize` closure runs pure and deterministic), then a daemon-only `*-vm` startup module after `T15`, copying the startup pattern `worldline-read-vm.ts` (`lararium-tw5`) holds, since ''Q'' burned `query-derive-vm.ts` (PR #149), with two new mesh subpath exports and an async channel round-trip. On the host binding stay the py and R pipe, the fs signal extraction, the coupling readers, the sense lifecycle verbs, the human-in-the-loop guard, telemetry and the palaces. TW5's boot leaves a startup whose `after` names an unrun task silently unrun, and a throw in `startup` kills the island, so the witness asserts the module's handle after boot and the body wraps its throw; new startup modules move the `filter-cts` goldens; TW5's `platforms` knows only browser and node, so daemon-only comes from plugin selection, which `T15` witnesses.
* `T15` The mirror witness: the glass mirror's plugin set never holds a daemon-only title.
* `T16` Injected homes, building on `CustodyHomes` and `vesselCustodyHomes()` (and `sealHome`, already a parameter through about 25 calls): retires `withLarRoot` (152 call sites), the CLI `--root` env mutation and the git-global shell-out. It also carries the daemon's no-argument genesis readers, which read only the `LAR_ROOT` env while `stand` spawns with `--root` and no `LAR_ROOT`, a split `L5`'s one resolver leaves standing. Mesh source reads no env. Needs `T2`; folds into or follows `T12`. Carries `T20`'s cure.
* `T17` Deadlines arrive injected, after the `dialDeadlines` precedent in `hearth-gate-pins.ts`: the 120 s and 3x pair (two literal copies, in the node composer and `daemon-vm-core.ts`) becomes one named deadline, and an absent deadline refuses rather than falling to the pool's 10 s default, which re-creates the fatal mount false-timeout. Two more fixed 10 s deadlines join the row: the teardown ack and the wiki place-verb. Red: a boot injecting 200 ms; control: the exact numbers at the pool constructor.
* `T18` Mutation as an inspection list, on `T1`'s recipe, in the long tier: diff-scoped runs with survivor lists and no score gate, an optional scoped incremental run on the box, the hand catalog kept beside it. Zero-kill tests become a review list, controls and seeds whitelisted, never an auto-delete. First survivors to answer, each red-first: `held >= floor` mutated to `held > floor` survives at `lares-cli` `kinds.ts` (an untested boundary); removing the `.sort()` in `quorum-entry.ts` survives (canonical parent order unasserted); the cycle-error text and the `?? []` defaults stand untested. Then the law pattern (fast-check, fixed seeds, a control, named mutants) extends to one more package, scored by the runner; `lararium-node`'s heavy suites take their own probe first. Adopting Stryker lands its lockfile delta (about 149 packages) in that lane. Unit shards and witness consolidation wait behind `T12`.

