!! Stride 1 Spine

Face and custody ground, then sealed identity and private authority; the face anchor precedes the planes that inherit it.

!!! Seven-league stride notes

* ''Integrity owed: face isolation, end to end'' (`K15` step 3, `B1`; `F6`'s slice three rides here with Wave B). Its witness: one adversarial multi-tab, multi-face run in a real browser, an unadmitted port, a stale generation, a cross-face sealed write and the last session's lock, where today only fake islands read them. MEASURED (the fresh read of Wave B; the readers, 2026-10-20). Wave B (PR #81) builds the guards and their reds on fake islands and the node; the one SharedWorker per house stands (`open-browser-vessel.ts`, `shared-holder-production.test.ts` on every engine that attaches one), and the real-browser adversarial run stays owed.
* ''Integrity owed: identity authority enforced, beyond the prose'' (`K15` step 6). Its witness: Wave C's red suite, a forged selector and a coherent foreign bundle refused, one sequence signed twice surfacing as a fork, a frontier that never falls. LEAD on the suite's shape; MEASURED that today's gate verifies continuity alone (`boot-daemon-keyhive.ts`).

!!! The rows

* `G7` Custody's edges on train N's ground: a short seat can write a charter that boots torn (`nexus-seal.ts`); a floor-class carrier standing alone founds, which decides whether a new custody adopts a standing vessel key (identity ground); `setFoundingRoute` stands as a test seam in source (`found.ts`). N.
* One charter per vessel rests on a single seal home (`larSealHome`), a guard on one file and never a law; a vessel that carries a second Nexus wants a second seal home, and the charter train names none.
* `K15` One hive per face (#/rulings, 2026-10-18): each PersonaGroup owns its Keyhive identity, event store, registry, archive and content-key seat, and no identity stands above them. Build order, each step red-first: (0) before bytes move, the custody contract of <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero`>>: the node and browser row census sorted D, F or S, the FCK key class, each face's own slot tree and recovery route, the carrier binding of face, row name and kind, and the overwrite contract generalized to a row-class key (#/rulings, a face's custody rows seal under its own key; a shared act never makes a shared secret) (the node census built, PR #70: each carrier row names its target classes, a LEAD mark and its open joint, and `encodeCarrierContext` spells the D and S seal context; the archive-row-selector joint traced and held open, PR #71: no archive site hands its row an authenticated PersonaGroup); (1) a substrate probe that two Keyhive instances in one process hold apart under interleaved acts, a reboot and a cross-read (measured: isolation holds, `packages/lararium-keyhive/tests/two-hives-one-process.probe.test.ts`), then a face context with its own store, registry, archive and key seat; (2) the face as the sole owner of its identity and group, the vessel's delegation gone from every face-bearing event (built, PR #68: `makeFaceBagDoor`, `faceOwnerVerifier`, a two-face event-byte capture its red, `W25`'s probe its regression), and 2b, a bag keeping one Document across boots (built, PR #68: `registerBagsDurably`, its record on the daemon doc for the vessel's ground and on each face's plane for that face's bags); the door grants the face's group before it records a Document (PR #69), so a crash between them re-enters to the same end; (2c, operator ruling 2026-10-19; built, PR #79) the atom cut: a random atom per (vessel, PersonaGroup) under that face's FCK signs every act on the face's behalf on node and browser, the place signer keeps the floor's duties alone, the wire subjects and verifiers move together, and its genesis, admit and founding-bootstrap deltas ride `X0` by `genesis/unbaked.json`, red-first on a thief holding the place seed deriving no veil and opening no group secret; on the local presence channel the session wears the mounted face, so a verb's presenter derives from the island's own atom and never from the CLI's unsigned `requestedBy`, the floor presents the place for floor acts alone, and a verb that names another face refuses by name (#/rulings, a session wears the face, 2026-10-11; a published atom key would link face and vessel on a wire); (3) sessions and registries routed by one face, no union, with `F6` slice three's asker-seals beside it, each sealer holding its row class's key (built, PR #81: the browser house keys by (PersonaGroup, persona root), the island proves each face through `gate:clear` while the holder holds no key, the island reads the fleet board's dyad itself, a fresh group mints a fresh atom, founding seeds key by their ask digest, and the node keys its atom and veil-archive rows by PersonaGroup digest; the daemon's last unions ride step 6); (4) content keys and removal per face, `K12`'s fresh group inside it; (5) a one-face restore and a herm that carries yet authors nothing; (6) the fence migration, identity bytes, split stores, slot trees and FCKs, and archive and custody formats together, under one identity model (#/rulings, sync carries, verification decides: the sealed anchor, the signed `@persona` log, verified projections): each D row (the atom's seed, its archive) seals under its face's FCK, where the node now seals them under the seated vessel key, and keys by its PersonaGroup, as the node's atom and veil-archive rows and the browser's atom row already do, where the browser's veil archive still keys by handle index. The isolation red: unlock face A alone, bypass every route, and try to open and replace B's occupied carriers with every key A holds, the S key included; each open fails, B's bytes stand unchanged, and A's bundle restored on a fresh vessel holds nothing of B. Steps (4) and (5) stay owed. K, W. Wave C (step 6 under the identity anchor, `readFace` as the one door with its census) landed in PR #86 on 2026-10-23. `K15-H` (the Handle owner rides the anchor, the row in `docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane`) landed in PR #88. Wave D (the FCK fence, its eight slices whole, kit `docs/pono/k15-wave-d-lane`) landed in PR #95 on 2026-10-26: each face seals its D rows under its own FCK, unlocks apart, bundles and restores alone, lifts its anon veil on join, and seats when its grant arrives. `K17`'s realm leg (`docs/pono/k17-realm-lease-lane`) landed in PR #97 on 2026-10-26. The bonds (kit `docs/pono/k15-bonds-lane`) landed in PR #106 on 2026-10-27: the place mints no Keyhive identity and its card retires; every face operation (dial, join, device edge, enrolment, sibling channel, daemon proof, group-secret open, `lares meme promote --face N`) signs or opens by the explicitly selected face's atom, a thief holding the place seed, face B or no face refusing at each gate on node and browser; a faceless floor boots no Keyhive and refuses face verbs by name; the relay key rests in its own random S row with the relay service its principal (`lares herm relay-rotate`); cadence takes a public key; the five floor duties sign through one scoped place-signer door; old mixed bytes refuse by name; and the seed census follows renamed carriers across calls, so every `K15` exception burned.
* `B1` Browser custody. The custody API stands specified in `browser-custody.ts`: a passphrase or paper (2-of-3) slot binds the slot tree, the device seed and every Keyhive Archive move into sealed carriers through the mesh's one sealed writer, a wrong route refuses and changes no byte, a locked keystore refuses `sealed-locked` before any mint, and the clear-password act asks through the confirm door and answers only to a literal yes. The boot stands (PRs #48 and #61): the vessel lock gives back on a throw and a `sealed-locked` boot retries in the same page, the web boot asks the unlock through its own form, the clear verb answers `asks` and calls no door before a literal yes, the wiki's `tm-clear-password` road asks through TW5's confirm road and writes no synced tiddler, the question names what it clears, and a declined unlock retries in the page. Under #/rulings (a shared act never makes a shared secret) the browser holds no vessel key, so the clear names one face and clears that face's rows, built inside `K15` steps 0 through 3. Owed: the persona roots, which still rest in the clear outside the tree, sealed under it, with the mint refusing until a slot binds (#/rulings); the browser's vessel-key rotation; and the passkey slot, after its derivation gets measured (`B3`) and never alone. Each tab asks for its own unlock, and the ask admits that tab to its face's open hive while the holder keeps a face's keys only while some session of that face stands unlocked (#/rulings, 2026-10-18; the research and its leads at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/session-unlock-2026`>>). Built with `K15` step 3 (PR #81): the holder answers a port only for a session it admitted, an unadmitted port asking for a sealed body refusing by name, and the last session of a face to close locks that face's hive; the production holder lifecycle runs on every engine that attaches the SharedWorker, and an engine that attaches none reads the floor and names why (`shared-holder-production.test.ts`). B.
* `W4` The face-scoped proof chain: face key, the vessel's face key, the session key. The subjects, private authority, the session signer and the session face supplier stand specified in code, and the withdrawal proof reads as a house model the operator may overturn (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-withdrawal-proof`>>). The two custody rows stand in node (`face-key-custody.ts`); fleet join calls the certificate and grant path, and `openJoinedFaceSession` stands. Owed: the browser holder of the face's custody rows. House. W. The browser's switch between faces rides here; the browser compose site reads its face's working slot from its keystore row (PR #108).
* `F12` A parallel draft names its writer by the record's own `modifier` value, else by the bare Automerge actor id; neither binds a face, so a reader learns only what a writer chose to say (`parallel-drafts.ts`). The session's face on each change answers it. O1.
* `F10` A person's fleet view and removal; the long-silent device rule of #/decisions. O1.
* `K12` A fresh PersonaGroup for a seat no hand can revoke (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/keys`>>). The PersonaGroup stands as a Keyhive group, so every other seat's revocation rolls the bags the group reaches (`persona-group-roll`); revoke authority follows the seating lineage, so a seat whose seating hand left, and the founder's own seat, leave only by a fresh group. Owed first: a name the face keeps across groups, since its plane names key on the group's id. It builds inside `K15`'s per-face removal step. K.
* `S7` Standing leans the seal met, kept as built unless the operator overturns one: an unlock mints a fresh Keyhive document for a binding whose floor-minted document died; one contact card per stand; the browser's creator veil stays unwired; a browser founded before the Keyhive move refuses to boot. Answered by rule and still open: a resumed face founding mints a new group; a founding stopped before its anchors re-founds with a fresh veil.
* `H5` An invited user's root mints on her device, sealed; the herm carries a sealed copy. B.
* `G13` Summons: no check of who wrote one; a consume tombstones every layer; a delivery claims its request id before it relays, so two deliveries of one pending summons place its verb once and a failed consume releases the claim (`verb-summons-claim.test.ts`), and the claim lives in memory (`verb-dispatcher.ts`, `verb-summons.ts`). Owed: a writer check, a working-layer tombstone alone, durable dedup, lease and fence, and honouring `aud`. House. G.
* `G34` A removal no reader can keep refuses by name (#/rulings; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/automerge-doc-store`>>). The store lands a based removal a concurrent writer overrode, then surfaces it to a listening reader alone: with no parallel-drafts reader it drops the surfacing with no word, and a reader that throws earns one console line while the write stands (`automerge-doc-store.ts`, `parallel-drafts.ts`). Owed: the refusal by name before any change lands, wherever no reader stands or every reader failed, with the store authoring no draft of its own; and the durable conflict handle the refusal carries (the document, the removal's request id, the conflicting change and head identities, never the hand's text), at a home where a hand whose editor went offline finds it again. G.
* `G35` The disk watcher's standing instruction (#/rulings; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/disk-projection#/projection-law`>>). Owed: the instruction as a record the operator signs by a human route, naming one bag, a path pattern and a per-wave count ceiling, which no automated seat signs; the watcher's settle of each pending removal it covers through the shore's removal door; the audit row that names the instruction a removal rode; `lares shore restore` over a settled removal; and a mass vanish past the ceiling, a standoff, or a removal outside the pattern left pending for a person (`packages/lares-cli/src/commands/watch.ts`, `shore-verb.ts`, `disk-projector.ts`). G.
* `K18` The recovery door: recovery-contact-quorum rotation of a persona root beneath its KEL prefix, then `reanchorAfterRotation`, then a re-admit carrying the current `@persona` log and signed frontier. Built in PR #135: enrolment takes exactly three recovery contacts at threshold two (#/rulings, 2026-10-31), signed into the enrolment and carried by every later rotation, each reveal opening three distinct keys at two, and the face's committed self-recovery digest counting as none of the three at a reveal. Owed: no production door rotates a root today, and the ceremony rotates under two of three recovery contacts; `reanchorAfterRotation` stands proven as a library function (Wave C, <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane`>> #/owed). It also closes `K17`'s window: a closed roster's keys can still raise the lease (stale more, never less) until this door rotates them out; the fold never lowers. K.
* `K16` The Teshima Family Council (#/rulings, 2026-10-18; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm`>>), `K15`'s acceptance story. Kalani founds a private council; Leilani joins it with two of her three faces. Red-first, after `K15`'s face context: (1) the council's hive as a Keyhive group holding no key of its own, its members the chosen faces' own identities; (2) an invite walks Leilani to the door, the threshold grafts each chosen face, a face leaves by its own act, and another's removal rides `kapae` or a fork by omission; (3) a member face's photo lands in its working layer of the council wiki and reaches the council's canon by `MOVE` (`W27`); (4) both chosen faces read it, the face kept back reads nothing and learns nothing, and no event in the council's history names a creator or issuer that ties two of Leilani's faces together; (5) a herm carries the sealed book and authors nothing (`K15` step 5). The e2e set stands four vessels: Kalani's, one per chosen face of Leilani's, and a herm. The e2e set walks the council at one hearth first: Kalani's seed charter holds the realm and Leilani's chosen faces walk there as guests, no Nexus founded (#/rulings, one charter). The two-hearth council follows, under the Nexus the two found, and there the member consult that lets a realm's documents cross between two operators reads a root map nothing fills (cabal-realm #/many-realms, owed), and the climb from seed charter to Nexus re-pins the realm by a named act (owed). Open joints: a quorum Handle with a seated key stands only where the council signs as one name, and that key signs collective acts alone, reaching no member's hive (#/the-steward-signer, owed). K, W.
* `K20` A face row's answer rides the socket alone (built in PR #131). Owed: the cabal-feed receipt's timing beside the leaf's slot write across the two daemon documents (a device-local ledger for sensitive act receipts); scrubbing a consumed summons; a caller-owned request id for `session:act` recovery; the maintenance frame's face-signing `realm-bag`. K; ahead of `K21`.
* `K21` Per-face content-key seats and mints, the end state that `K19`'s fence holds the place for: each joined face seals its own content keys, holds its own outbox and mints its own bags, so a verb stops running on the mounted face's resources whichever provider cleared it. It carries `U1`'s named regression: sibling devices of one face read none of each other's seals, since `holdsWrite` accepts only this vessel's own chain until the grant ring reads by face key. It rests on sealed-store step 3 and answers through the socket-only shape of `K20`. K.
* `P1` The steward signer: the composing vessel's `realm-bag` verb calls the steward door (`realm-steward.ts`); the docker `meme` scenario by hand, in the asker's order; a door for a collective Handle's seal waits on the chartered classes; the vouch door, the feed's writer and a realm's holder hand sign with the worn face's key at the Nexus the realm stands under (`cabal-face.ts`). P.
* `P9` The re-seal proof and the fork-resolve act stand ruled (#/rulings): the re-seal record builds with sealed-store step three, the fork-resolve act in train N.
* `P13` Per-meme grants; a leaf honouring a session's effective recipe. O1 for the recipe.
* `I3` The intent plane under re-pin, re-target and growth (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane`>>; built on `I1` and `I2`; the once-under-re-pin half built in PR #132). Owed, each red-first with its control: the cross-device fence (S2); the receipt's one-digest heads (S3); the class audience in production and the issuer's own cancel and supersede (S4); the pane's and `intent show`'s denials, `outOfAudience` outcomes and refusal ids, a signed fault record and a finite `every` that waits (S5); compaction (S6). Relay.
* `W9` The sibling channel at face scope, on per-dial transport keys. W.
* `W12` The herm route for cancel and the three receipts, as ruled (#/rulings; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/receipt-ledger#/the-relay-leg`>>); no code asks, cancels or answers across a herm. Owed, with `W9`: the ask, the cancel and the vessel's answer as a tagged inner frame under the sealed sibling session's own seal, the vessel reading that session's proof as the asker's; the herm's bare delivery note inside the session, bound to the ask's unique request id and the session's causal position, attesting transit and never execution; and the rule for which verbs a sibling's standing reaches across the session (`sibling-channel.ts`, `uds-channel.ts`). W.
* `E2` The serving key's custody and its unattended road (#/rulings, the ember's key at rest; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-table`>>). Built: the fifth class `serving` in the carrier table, read by the census and `vault status`; SK minted at the founding; `sk-slots` with the vessel key's entry, opened at every human unlock and re-wrapped by a vessel-key rotation. Owed: the serving rows under SK and SK's own rotation; no minting secret in any serving row; the anchor path, where an ember slot answers unattended only against a hardware-sealed hearth key whose attestation the ember checks on each ask; the confirm path, where every slot of a hearth with no such anchor answers only on a person's confirm and threshold two asks a second confirm, never an unattended raise; and the bare deny-only `sk-rotation-owed` mark that any counted removal sets and that refuses every ask until SK rolls (`vault-carriers.ts`, `keyslot.ts`, `custody-seat.ts`). E.
* `E3` The serving gate's tier (#/rulings, the ember's serving gate; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-gate-exchange`>>). Owed: a third tier name in the route type, its bundle derived from SK under its own registered domain, its pin, and a pin's move by a signed causal event or a verified key-history step alone, with no quiet period that ages a pin out (`gate-bundle.ts`). E.
* `E4` The raise's commit point and its lapse (#/rulings, how a raise lapses; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/waking-floor#/the-shape`>>). Owed: the count spent at the raise ledger's durable commit, before SERVING composes, so a crash before the commit spends nothing and serves nothing and a crash after it burns the raise; and the raise's lapse at a lock, a restart, a human unlock or a counted removal, with no timer and no heartbeat that ends it (`custody-seat.ts`, the raise ledger's writer). E.
* `H2` The delegation and three dials stand specified in `hosting-delegation.ts`. Owed: the live issuer, reader, hosting store and socket sorter in one signed-act cut. H.
* `H8` The grant's signed shape and public-half verifier stand specified in `walker-grant.ts` (#/rulings; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/ember#/the-tiers`>>). Owed: the live roll that derives grant public halves for serving rows inside H's one act cut, before E's walker arm. H.

