!! Stride 2 Floor

Floor, wire and realm release shapes on the face and authority ground.

!!! Seven-league stride notes

* ''The floor's trust chain'' (`W14`, `W15`, `W16`: the signed floor card, the pin's causal position, carry-floor convergence) stands built, PR #100, witnessed by the rotation-and-carry storm (`place-claim-storm`) that accepts no stale pin and converges the same way on every carrier.
* ''Research pair: the Keyhive substrate's contract'' (`W11`, filed after the seat). Its question: which substrate properties stand as contract and which shift by version, each needing a guard at run time. Lenses: dependency contract analysis / adversarial compatibility testing.
* ''Research pair: the knock's leak'' (`W10`; its answer moves the dial's bytes, so it lands before the bake). MEASURED (two traded rounds, then a Mu test on the web, 2026-10-26; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w28-gate-lane`>> #/the-knock-reading): IK already stands, so a dialer proves itself before any verdict; the floor knock harms nothing the floor promises; on the sovereign route a reader holding candidate pins and the clear path learns which of the K gates sharing an address and route a dial selects, at most log2(K) bits per dial, never the face, the verdict or a sealed byte; no public-pin filter escapes that, and a secret selector costs per-Nexus key delivery and a causal re-key on every removal. The operator ruled (2026-10-26) that the sovereign promise leaves a pin-holding path reader outside it, so `W10` closes as a named leak, with more research owed later.

!!! The rows

* `W26` The system wikis release and every other wiki reads the floor (#/rulings, 2026-10-16). Slice 1 stands (PR #49): genesis carries the first floor, its manifest and the `lares` and `lararium` snapshots by CID, and `@oracle` reads that floor by CID. Slice 2 stands (PR #52): each vessel's system, crossroads and realm pointers rest in its own `@catalog`, and nothing writes the shared `@oracle` after genesis (`oracle-doc-no-writer.test.ts`). Slice 3 stands (lane `--w26-floor-3`): the founding lands the counted 1-of-1 Kahu admission for persona zero's group (`landFoundingAdmission`) and registers `lares` and `lararium` as realm bags of the hearth's realm under persona zero's per-Nexus key (`landKahuRealm`); `kahuCabalCanonAccess` has its production caller (`kahuReachSourceOf`); the keel mounts only what the realm names, the registered bag set and the `bags/` mirrors follow, and no catalog row names a system bag. Slice 6 stands: one predicate (`requireKahuReach`) guards the residency reactor, meme put and delete, draft placement and a realm steward's write, and the keyholder island's verifier carries it for `--in-wiki` verbs. Slice 4 stands: the release (`floor-release`: body, CID, steward seal by a seated Kahu key, the cabal's high-impact approval of the manifest's exact bytes, the charter's epoch lineage), the chain fold, `lares nexus release`, the porch (`GET /floor/<Nexus AID>`, `/cas/<cid>` for the head's blobs), the browser's verified read, and the flow map's own `flow-pointer` domain in place of the retired `oracle-pointer`. Slice 5 stays owed: no source holds the accept act. The build runs six slices in order, under the architecture of #/rulings (2026-10-18), its shape and evidence at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane`>>: (1) the floor manifest and its read-face, genesis baking the first floor; (2) each vessel's pointers leave the shared document for its bootstrap, re-cutting `W21`; (3) the Kahu realm holds the live system documents, and a one-seat founding lands its 1-of-1 Kahu admission; (4) the release answer on the crossroads, folding `P8`; (5) the accept act per (face, Nexus), which rides the face context since its accepted floor rests as a face's D row; (6) reach into system canon refuses every hand outside the cabal. OWED: a browser Kahu hand rides the face context (the browser composes no board reader and reads as a stranger, fail closed); a sibling device of a seat-holding face reads the floor until that context carries the charter and the board to it, and `device-admit.ts` states the law; a joinee reads its hearth's floor by the release and its CIDs (slice 4), where slice 5's accept act moves its pin; the carriage `canon` names (`device-admit.ts` `admitCanonDocs`, the browser's `hearth-canon`) read rows nothing writes, and retire with this row. W.
* A floor read carries no as-of stamp: `standAs` returns a bare class (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/waking-floor`>>).
* The hostful code half: `carrierBaseRelPath` discards a hostful URI (`bag-paths.ts`), so a hostful title never sites; one carrier claims otherwise (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/lar-uri-namespace`>>).
* `G20` Carried items, each now owned (porch, PR #105, kit `docs/pono/porch-lane`). Closed: the sensorium's tree-sitter pins (`tree-sitter==0.26.0`, ABI 15 inside its window, pinned by test) and the corpus round-trip, which now sweeps every carrier under `bags/` and fails by name on one skipped by shape. Ruled by the house on the porch's leans, built in the porch's next bundle: road (iv) surfaces the derived impact set for review as information, while a quorum revokes by name; a loan keys by CID, keeping holder and tier, once the loan carries a causal expiry; `/cas` lands and verifies the body before the public index names it. The cold-boot grace retired with `K15`'s bonds (PR #106): `resolveBootDoc` waits on the writer's own flush, never a clock. The parallel-draft alert's persistence passes to the hands room. G.
* `P10` The vessel-side fetch door stands built (`makeCidResolver` beside `hermCasTransitFromEnv` in `open-node-vessel.ts`); the herm's own client leg waits on the explicit-Nexus herm relay, since a herm dials no hearth. One circle in the law stands beside it: a carrier may read a book its registration declares public, the declaration lives on the realm doc, and the realm doc never crosses to a carrier. The held red in `tests/e2e/herm-reshares-public-blob.e2e.test.ts` waits on both. Also owed: seeding a herm from a stood Lararium. House. Before the fence where the ceremony seeds a herm.
* `P11` Board migration beyond the persona log; the explicit DEPARTURE, named by an act at the rite and never inferred at a boot; the offering's announce and taker doors. May follow.
* `P12` A realm's edge board and vouch board cross by a lane of their own, and a fleet's edge board by the sibling lane; both composers have yet to seat those lanes (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/four-edges`>>). May follow.
* The Handle surface adapters: four surfaces stand as type and vocabulary; loopback first, then DNS control (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/handle-card`>>). `lares handle graft` stands as a stub over a built mint, where `publish`, `rotate`, `burn` and `attest` run live; the antigen's ban-`nym` move stays untouched; the browser's publish surface and a phone summons that presents the veil card stay owed. Flagged, unbuilt: a Handle's presenting cabal may also serve as its recovery cabal.
* `K9` The cadence lineage's seat events and its offer verifier; the joint founding's one cadence citation stands, and a household seed cites none (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu#/contract`>>). P, with the offers.
* `W29` The place signs by a scoped signer under a pre-rotated KEL (#/rulings, the place signs by a scoped signer, 2026-10-19; kit <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane`>>): built, PR #98, 2026-10-26. One KEL grammar (`vessel-kel.ts`, beside `persona-kel` and `handle-kel`): the inception seats the online signer and commits a cold next-key digest; a rotation reveals that key, which signs it, seats a replacement signer and commits a fresh next key; no interaction events. Every founding door, node, hearth, herm kindle and browser alike, mints the armed inception and lands no byte before the founding card reads back through the `PlaceFoundingCard` port, and the cold seed rests on no file. `lares vessel rotate` runs the card ceremony: it verifies the old card against the head, reads the replacement card back, then stages, publishes and reconciles under one custody claim, and a restart never invents a successor. Peers learn the head from the Nexus carriage board and an offline herm from the carry bundle; one fold, bounded at 64 rows and 8 pieces of fork evidence per AID, refuses a gap, a rollback and a fork. The five floor duties sign and verify `len(D) ‖ D ‖ preimage`. A seed census names every raw-seed consumer and fails on a new one. Owed: a browser ceremony UI that seats a card (until it lands, the browser's KEL door refuses by name and a browser leaf holds no place KEL). Since `W14`–`W16` (PR #100), the floor pin duty and the carrier seal resolve their signer at the head (`verifyPlaceDutyAtHead`, `verifyCarrierContractAtHead`), and a flow pointer reads its publisher off the verified head; since `K15`'s bonds (PR #106), no seed reaches past the floor and the census reads no exception. W.

