!! Stride 3 Bake

The one labelled re-bake and rename, followed by the founding format cut.

!!! Seven-league stride notes

* ''Integrity owed: the bake's cross-product'' (`X0`, touching `K15` step 6, `W26`, `G37`). Its witness: one matrix over the pre-bake and post-bake artifacts, every old CID refused after the bake and a fresh two-of-two founding standing, rather than greens read row by row.
* ''The refold's bound'' (`G15`) stands built: a roll storm completes in bounded passes, one holder at a time, with no overlap and no starved holder (`after-roll-chain.test.ts`).
* ''Integrity owed: the habit flip at the bake'' (`X0`, `G37`). Before the bake the house runs re-genesis freely, since no CRDT document survives; after it, a re-genesis costs every CID a second operator pins. Its witness: a census of each instrument, fixture, brief and runbook line that assumes a free re-genesis, each named to flip or retire inside the bake's own commit, never after it.

!!! The rows

* `G37` The evergreen sweep of 2026-10-18 (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/evergreen-sweep-2026`>>, its six rulings and fourteen lanes). Built: (1) the standing witness `tools/evergreen-boundary.mjs` (PR #53), its per-rule ceilings, which only come down, living in that file and nowhere in prose; (8) the engine watch reads an engine by its sha256 (PR #60); (5) worldline replay orders by parent links and handle dependencies and names every skip (PR #62), the mempalace KG still dropping `parentKey` when it persists and the CLI tree's sequential mark still reading recorded times, each exception naming its rule, file, line, count and reason; (2) `bytesEqual`, `constantTimeBytesEqual`, a strict `hexToBytes` and `nexusAidOfPin` in `@lararium/mesh` (PR #51). Order of the rest: (3) opaque ids, the mount nonce, optional display times and parent-link worldline replay, after `W26` slice 2, the clock sinks at effect-record, residency-actions, sense-sensorium, handler-args, engine-watch, wiki-behavior, verb-tiddler and vessel-mailbox; (4) the engine watch by CID, the `LarDoc` and session-envelope shapes, the floor announcement's kind and the browser store's current shape; (5) the numbered preimages and formats renamed together in the bake that closes `W26`, the signing preimages outside `domains.ts` among them (holder-continuity, persistence-keel, wax-stamp's `lar-*/v1`), which take the same frozen-preimage ruling as `engine/v1`. Each lane red-first under a clock set to 1970 and to 3000. G.
* `X0` The founding bake: one deliberate re-genesis before a second operator stands, after which CIDs are meant to last because another operator pins them. It moves together `K15` step 6 (identity bytes, split stores, slot trees and FCKs, archive and custody formats, each face's random device veil), the place KEL's pre-rotation and the scoped place signer (the signer frames each duty's domain itself, signing `len(D) ‖ D ‖ preimage` and its verifiers the same, so no signed floor image carries its own separation; built with `W29`, whose readiness red reads a fresh genesis founded armed and the five framed pairs verifying), `W26`'s closing bake (the floor release), and `G37`'s preimage and format renames (`engine/v1` and its kin, the floor announcement's kind, the genesis seed and CAS formats). Each member carries its own readiness red, so the bake waits on the slowest by name, never on a date; the bake's own red: a fresh genesis founds, and no CID from before the bake verifies after it. A cut re-founds and recognises no bytes from before it (#/rulings, old shapes burn); boundary guards get designed after the founding. The gate it opens: a second operator may found a Nexus fresh at two of two. X.

