!! After The Seat

Remaining behavior, proof, interface and later-plane work after the second-seat shape fence.

!!! Seven-league stride notes

* ''Shelf note'': `F6`'s slice three rides Wave B on the spine; slice four (the daemon kernel into the holder) stays here.

!!! The rows

* `G6` The evergreen sweep's remainder on held ground: stale prose, back-compat wording and tolerant readers in files other lanes hold, each named with its owner in the ground lane's shape file (`open-node-vessel.ts`, `open-browser-vessel.ts`, `nexus-seal-seed.ts`, `seed-wrap-prf.ts`, the tolerant readers in `ingest-core.ts`, `lar-uris.ts`, `mesh-palace.ts`). G; the false source comments ride the code lane of #/side-lanes.
* `G8` Measures. The per-verb flush stands measured by `tools/flush-bench.mjs`, a flush microbenchmark over the 443 resident carriers (porch, PR #105); its reading rests in the porch kit, never here. Owed: pack-PIN recursion stands unbuilt, and `assertBodyIndexTier` gains its production caller with the body-index writer. G.
* `G18` The shore: the mode row never moves. G or B.
* `G19` Canon sweeps. The porch read the shore surface's carriers, the test door's scratch marker, the browser surface's secure-context law and `secure-context.mem#/behind-the-terminator` against the code and harbor's law, and found them agreeing (PR #104). Owed: `kahu.mem` and `lamplighters.mem` on what the code holds, which waits on the operator's cadence-share intent (#/open). G.
* `G27` A wiki island that stands live and unpinned takes no `lares shore` answer: the shore verb reaches the active wiki's island and the daemon island (`askShore`, `packages/lares-cli/src/shore-core.ts`), and a person settles a standoff in another live island by bringing the two sides to say the same. G.
* `S2` The fold's live proof on the rebuilt image, with a pushed shard run reading green. S.
* `A10` The Pronaos household proof: one reserved docker project that attributes the arrival bytes to their shore and the node faces to their owners, then fresh browser peers through relay and oracle loss. A.
* `A11` A pushed head of this branch whose held-out reading shows every driver green (`node tools/ci-verdict.mjs`, the third reading). A.
* `A12` An unlock spends its time in three boots of the wiki engine, and the terminal shows nothing meanwhile. One instrumented run on a marked scratch root, pinned to one core, with the genesis corpus alone: the key derivation takes under two seconds; the sovereign composition then takes about six to reach `corpus-ready`, seven from the `[dyad]` line to the daemon island's `working layer attached`, and four to `tw5-booted`. An unlock sent while the floor's own daemon island still boots waits that boot out first, six seconds more, so the first unlock after a restart answered in twenty-eight seconds where a later one answered in fifteen. The span a person met past eighty seconds sits at the same `[dyad]` line, so it scales with the corpus the daemon island boots over. No small cure reads here. Owed: a progress line per phase at the unlocking terminal, and a measurement over a full workspace corpus. The compose owner's boot path. A.
* `A13` A staged container that restarts after its boot's founding act wrote the seed charter and before it lit persona zero's face loses the staged card: the next boot's act completes the face, the charter already stands, so no card returns, and the kahu roll under `LAR_STAND_KAHU` skips with its warning (`tools/lararium-container-boot.sh`, the `LAR_STAND_FACE` founding and the roll after it). It binds disposable staged roots alone: a household founding prints its card on the terminal and keeps no copy. A.
* `K8` The face-proof gate reads the admitted key's hand-over line, as the socket gate does. The key and its line stand built: a face's per-Nexus key mints at random into its sealed row and re-issues by a hand-over the carriage board carries (`nexus-leaf.ts`, `lares persona reissue`; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-key-hierarchy`>>). The remainder rides the socket cutover. W.
* `K13` The sealed outbox (#/rulings; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-table`>>). Parcels rest sealed under random names in the `outbox` class. Owed: carriage shipping, idempotent receipt and local delete after ship. K.
* `K14` The restored face's provisional standing (#/rulings; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-restore`>>). The mark, recovery contact or chair view, confirm verbs and three authority-changing refusals stand. Owed: provisional guards at the root-signed crossing, edge kapae, device admit, two-founder act and session signer's authority purpose; a sibling view needs independent proof; the recovery contacts' path where every party stays unreachable. K, W, N.
* `N5` A newcomer's board catch-up of acts it never saw stands outside the witnessed charter re-import along one lineage. N, X.
* `P3` Many realms: the cross-operator member consult of a cabal realm waits on the face-scoped proof subject and on the vouch door naming a worn face's key. P, W.
* `P8` One public answer per Nexus, signed by the steward: the floor release answer, built as `W26`'s release slice (#/rulings, 2026-10-18): the body, the steward's seal, the approval and the porch stand (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu`>> #/floor-release). The domain's Handle table stays here, off the ceremony's chain by ruling. P, W.
* `P17` The realm feed's writer check: the feed verb runs in the daemon island (`cabal-realm-verbs.ts`), while the worn face's key at a realm's Nexus mints on the vessel's main thread behind the custody door (`cabal-face.ts`), so the verb resolving its own writer needs a door from the island to the vessel, the shape of `dyad:ask`, which moves the capability inventory and the compose files. The one production caller, `lares cabal feed`, names that key through `cabal-face`; the residue: a caller that types any writer. P.
* `P18` The shared-canon read consults `kahuCabalCanonAccess`, admission AND sentinel membership. The node daemon consults it through `kahuReachSourceOf` (`operator-daemon-behavior.ts`: naming a system canon's live document, every write, the intent verifier); at every other reader a removed group keeps its Keyhive sentinel capability (`boot-daemon-keyhive`). Both vessels' daemon payloads (`open-node-vessel.ts`, `open-browser-vessel.ts`) carry the group and sentinel ids alone, so each composition threads the Nexus AID, the seated roster and the carriage board into the read together; a node-only gate leaves the browser reader open. P.
* `P19` Cabal acts across a roll: an act counts only under the epoch it names, so after a seal roll standing reads `absent` until the seats re-admit at the new head; anchored ancestry, which `lares nexus members` reads, carries them, and an `onRolled` refold for the cabal verbs follows once a live reading folds them. It follows `P20`'s writer rule, and its cabal half rests parked on the branch `--gate-ancestry`. P.
* `W10` The knock tests offline for a reader holding candidate pins and the clear path (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/gate-bundle.ts`, `knockSegment`, `gateKnock`): CLOSED as a named leak by the operator's ruling (2026-10-26), the sovereign route's promise leaving a pin-holding path reader outside it (face-proof #/named-leaks; the reading at `docs/pono/w28-gate-lane` #/the-knock-reading). More research owed later: whether a secret selector, its first-dial bootstrap and its causal re-key on every removal earn their cost, read again when a sovereign pin escapes its members' custody, when route confidentiality against pin-holders enters the promise, or when hearths commonly stand many Nexuses behind one address; a flip after `X0` moves the dial's URL bytes by its own versioned rite. W, canon.
* `W11` Keyhive keeps the PersonaGroup's private membership and carries no face chain: four probe readings on 0.3.0-alpha.1 stand as alarms (`packages/lararium-keyhive/tests/face-chain-substrate.probe.test.ts`), and a Keyhive bump re-reads them. House. W.
* `W19` A fleet-join carry walk in the browser weld; the weld's anchored walks await their port. W.
* `W22` `composeCasTransits` in `node-cas.ts` shapes `P10`'s client leg and gets wired; `openBrowserVessel`'s `walkInvite` option stands without a caller, while the CLI's `walkInvite` runs `walk invite`. W.
* `W23` The floor-crossing CI cell (`packages/lararium-web` `vitest.crossing.config.ts`, about seven minutes under chromium) reads the browser floor crossing on every push: the `floor-crossing` job in `.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs it under a scratch HOME, LAR_ROOT and LAR_STAGE_DIR, and `tools/vitest-config-callers.test.mjs` fails any named vitest config that no workflow, tool or package script runs. W.
* `W24` `herm-reshares-public-blob` walks a public user book (PR #55): the fleet mints `herm-public-photo` on A and registers it public on the realm; step ③ LOADs the blob into the book's working slot and promotes it into canon by `MOVE` through the island `W27` opens; step ④ reads C, a second vessel of A's own face joined by `fleet join`, listing the book with A's doc id through its stood realms; steps ⑤b and ⑦ name an unstaged blob, and ⑦'s shut holds. Owed beside: readiness entries (a wiki mounted with its layers laid) and a per-carrier entry, so a script awaits a second write too; the daemon's reach waits on a bag's document the way the kernel's slot wait does, instead of one bounded find; a guard on the event route's order; a CLI that gives up on its budget cancels its waiter. W.
* `F1` The scoped document view stands specified in mesh (`session-document-view.ts` over `gated-sync-leg.ts`); the pool's surface door (`mountSurface`) and the island kernel's half ride it, and no production caller mounts a surface. Owed: every interactive surface mounts under it in place of the broad sync port, which waits on a verified face (train W) and on callers that hold a session (`F4`, `F6`); the face-fleet-view bridge stands as a narrow share caller today, and O1 replaces it with per-surface facets that keep an owner from offering a session island a document beyond them; an admitted leaf's relay adapter wears the one-way gate over its hearth's canon documents, and the hearth wears that gate's twin toward its leaves (`hearth-canon.ts`, `open-browser-vessel.ts`, `open-node-vessel.ts`); a wiki island's verbs that read the catalog document move to the view's catalog ask. O1.
* `F2` One recipe resolver (`surface-recipe.ts`) and the pool keyed by the whole session key (`mountSurface`) stand specified in mesh, with one proof through the node vessel's own parts that a recipe naming an offering resolves. Both platforms select plugins through its `resolveRecipePluginCids`; no production caller reaches `resolveSurfaceRecipe`. Owed: the node and browser compose sites resolve through the one function at surface mount; the wiki door (`mountWiki`), its retained mount specs and the recipe watch retire with the last caller; a surface island's events reach a verb gate bound to its session (`onSurfaceEvent`) when the node callers move (`F4`). O1.
* `F6` The browser holder as owner, with unicast replies. Slice one stands (PR #56): a closed routing table (`holder-routes.ts`) sends each island message to exactly one port, a reply by its request id, camera traffic by its lease, the island's own asks to its owner port, and drops a kind with no route by name. Slice two stands (PR #58): every tab-to-holder message rides a random owner epoch, a session and a generation, and the holder refuses a stale or unknown one by name to that port alone; `session:open` with its face waits on `W4`'s face supplier. Slices three and four move the Repo and the daemon kernel into the holder; their sealed writes go to the asker (#/rulings, the asker seals). Slice three stands with `K15` step 3 (PR #81): the holder routes each sealed write to the session that caused it, and Chromium, which exposes no nested Worker inside a SharedWorker, takes the dedicated-worker floor, its swap waiting for the worker's `ready` before it replays the manifest and retiring the crossing it replaces. Slice four stays owed. O1.
* `H1` The operator's answer and the door that shows what waits. `lares host` stands with `roll` and `invite`, and bare `lares host` reads each hosted Nexus's epoch, cap and redemptions (`host-cmd.ts`). Owed: `host answer` and the reader of the walkers that wait. H.
* `H3` A walker's token buys a knock unless pre-answered (`socket-sorter.ts`). H.
* `H4` The strangers' dial. H.
