The o-takiage rite of 2026-10-20 moves these complete rows here, and every land since moves its own; each row names nothing still owed by that row.

* `T20` ''A login flip mints a second persona root'' (custody). Custody file names carry the git global email: `readLocalOperatorHint` shells it with a 2 s timeout and swallows every error (its 11 catch wrappers never fire), and 13 call sites re-shell. A flip (timeout, unset `HOME`, `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL`, an edited email) lets `generateOrLoadPersonaGroupRoot` mint a second root with no founding card, orphaning the first; a `found` on a flipped login mints a second key and KEL. The vessel key's own mint stays guarded by the founding-card read-back. The suffix retires and custody resolves its home once at open (#/the-floor; the census already reads every suffix as one custody). Red: mint a root under one email, flip it, assert the next call refuses by name; control: the unchanged config loads. Lane `recut-custody` (the stride notes). Landed, PR #138 (`3726248e5`): fixed custody names inside the one custody home; the operator's re-found notice rides the PR.
