* `K17` The edge frontier (#/rulings, the edge frontier, 2026-10-20). Red-first: the frontier certificate and its verifier on node and browser alike; the signed empty genesis at every founding; registration of a raise into its signer's next frontier; the widening reader (admit, grant, a content-key seal) acting as of a qualifying frontier and waiting as unknown otherwise; the admit bundle carrying the frontier and its snapshot; the reader persisting its highest accepted head. Reds: a withheld first raise, a deleted local raise, a stale clean frontier, two conflicting frontiers, a missing snapshot, a concurrent raise and lower, an epoch rollover. K. The fleet board's frontier stands built with Wave C. The realm leg, K17-R (kit `docs/pono/k17-realm-lease-lane`, the operator's rulings on forks 3 and 4, 2026-10-22), landed in PR #97 on 2026-10-26: one lease law, so a Nexus or realm lease rises only on a charter quorum's signed advance read under its seal-epoch lineage and the unsigned max-register retires with no reader left; each voucher signs its own hand's frontier; a seal roll signs every anchored realm's head under the new epoch; a split-seat cosign carries its head; and the realm admit bundle carries the board's acts, frontiers and snapshots, so a joiner holding no board acts as of them. The closed roster's window passes to `K18`.
