* `F8` The control-event leg stands built: `lar:control-event` and `lar:control-result` replace `wiki:dom-event` and `wiki:dom-input` (`lar-camera.ts`, `projection-sink.ts`). The porch burned the guard in `lar-wire.test.ts` (PR #102); D2 burned the last, in `projection-input-leg.test.ts` (PR #103). O1.
* `F3` One working document per (face, wiki, slot kind) at a face-secret address. O1. Built in PR #108 (kit `docs/pono/hands-spine-lane`): the face's address secret mints at its founding behind custody, the working document derives from it by wiki and slot kind on node and browser, a restored face carries the secret in its bundle, and a floor with no face seated keys its working document by the place until the join lifts it.
* `F4` Node callers move to sessions; receipts bind to the face; verb outcomes and the effect index follow the working layer with their reader (`verb-vm.ts`, `uds-channel.ts`). O1. Built in PR #108 (kit `docs/pono/hands-spine-lane`): every store-door row and sealed act that acts as a face rides a session of that face, a row naming another face refuses `face-row-other-face`, and the receipt binds the face's proof subject.
* `F5` The durability receipt, rung 2's node half. O1. Built in PR #108 (kit `docs/pono/hands-spine-lane`): a durable outcome rests under the face's proof subject and the input digest, and a later session of the same face reads it.
* `F9` The switch; the vessel-wide selector retires. Its one persisted shape, the selector's two stores (the node's active-persona index and the browser's `ACTIVE_PERSONA_STORE`), retired with `K15` Wave D (PR #95): the worn face lives as session state on node and browser, and no store keeps it. The switch act itself lands additive. O1. The switch stands built in PR #108 (kit `docs/pono/hands-spine-lane`): `session:switch` runs a five-step fence that moves one session alone, and `lares persona wear` retired with the vessel-wide selector; a command names its face (`--face N`) or reads the one face standing open.
* `A8` `persona wear` on a standing vessel waits on the session switch. O1. Closed in PR #108: `persona wear` retired; a session switches in place.
* `W17` Face switching on one device, and a second joined face on one vessel. House. W. Built in PR #108 (kit `docs/pono/hands-spine-lane`): each joined face opens its own session and switches in place; the daemon judging a second face's atom as that face rides `K19`.
* `K19` One Keyhive provider per joined face at the daemon (operator ruling, 2026-10-27; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract#/the-hands`>>). Built, PRs #110, #118, #121 and #127 (kit `docs/pono/k19-hive-lane`): each unlocked joined face boots its own provider over its own event-store scope and routes by the presenter's atom key; the content fence denies by default; content cannot claim the channel; a session acts only as the face it wears; and the realm feed binds to the face→leaf bond. What stays owed rests in `K20` and `K21`, and a council's quorum Handle stays with `K16`. K.
* `I2` The far agent's relay seat: the least relay trust and attestation that stops capability escalation and argument substitution while keeping causal provenance. Built, PRs #112 and #125 (kit `docs/pono/i2-relay-lane`): delegation and revoke ride the plane, admission leaves the entry unchanged and rides beside it as a receipt, both composers register a face's planes only as its signed log names them, a malformed sibling row leaves only its own face unread, and the SharedWorker holder listens before it loads. What stays owed rests in `I3`. I.
* `T1` The Stryker probe (measured 2026-10-31, lane `stryker-probe`, a local branch never pushed): StrykerJS 10.1.1 with its vitest runner activates and kills mutants under vitest 5.0.3, picking the `>` test-name separator, so the earlier no-mutant reading retires. On `lares-cli` (`kinds.ts`, `engine.ts`) 994 mutants score 72.7% in 812 s at concurrency 4 (876 MB sandbox, 690 MB peak); an unchanged incremental rerun takes 31 s; a `lararium-mesh` slice (`cap-compose.ts`, `quorum-entry.ts`) scores 86.1% in 16 s. The suites kill a Stryker mutant on all 14 hand-catalog lines; Stryker reproduces about 9 of their shapes and cannot generate the operand swap, the statement insertion or the template reorder, so the catalog keeps its job. Recipe: run from the repo root, `inPlace` false, the runner's `pool` set to `forks` (its own default `threads` overrides the suites'), the sandbox lacking gitignored `dist/` and untracked files, any failing dry-run test aborting the run. `lararium-node` stays unprobed. T.
* `L5` Cold start reaches the genesis seed (walk gap G5). A founding reads `LAR_GENESIS`, else `<LAR_ROOT>/genesis` (`found.ts`), and nothing stages it, so a cold root takes a hand copy. Built, PR #143 (`ec3c990be`): one genesis resolver serves the daemon, `main.ts` and the CLI, so a cold root reaches the build's shipped genesis with no hand copy while an explicit `LAR_GENESIS` still wins, and a shipped-seed founding pins its seed CID, the pin moving only on a successful founding. What stays owed rests in `T16` (the daemon's no-argument readers) and the porch (the pin's crash window). L.
* `T19` ''Carried posture goes stale'' (security, public shelf, strangers only). A refold drops no-longer-held sockets synchronously and then fires the gate re-sweep un-awaited, so the drop always sorts on the previous sweep's posture: a carried Nexus tightening from open to private keeps seated strangers until a later refold, and a knock in the gap sorts stale. The realm-plane refold drops with no re-sweep at all; `unstand()` (`face-gate-server.ts`) closes no seated socket; sweeps run unserialized, so an older read can land last and re-stand a gate, while the intent relay serializes and shuts every gate on a read failure. Cure: refresh the readings, then drop, as one owned step on both refold paths; serialize the sweeps; shut on a read failure. Red: tighten a carried charter with a stranger seated, refold, assert the socket closes in that refold; controls: an own-Nexus flip, the herm staying open. Lane `recut-gates`, both slices (the stride notes). Landed, PR #141 (`5535ebe8c`): one owner for a vessel's gate sweep (`gateSweep`, a transport-free mesh stage) refreshes the carried postures, drops what they demote, then moves the gates, on both refold paths; a gate stood down cuts the sockets it seated. What stays owed rests in the porch (the composer's cell order, the rig's notes).
* `T22` ''Share inputs withhold until they stand'' (defense in depth). `kahuProtected`, `antigenRing` and `edgeShadows` allow while null; only the build order (`T6`) keeps a peer from arriving first, and Automerge's share policy allows everything by default, so the house guard stands as the only deny layer. Each null input withholds by name. Also the floor-on-a-stale-store case: a floor booting on a store left by an earlier sovereign run reads the old Kahu documents unclassed; red: the share verdict with empty protected ids, a dialed peer and the Kahu canon id must deny. On the lane that red read green (a locked floor's holder reads incomplete, and the guard withholds all), so the clause retires at the lane's land. Lane `recut-gates`, slice 1. Landed, PR #141: a share input that has not stood withholds by name from wire and sibling peers, and every keel names its system canon.
* `T27` ''Teardown seams''. A refused boot leaves a stale cas door; the sync gates carry no torn-down guard, so a sweep in flight during teardown can register a route that makes the next composition throw "already owned" and stand no gates until restart; the custody and dyad doors drop before the daemon island shuts. Lane `recut-gates`: the refused boot's door in slice 1, the rest in slice 2. Landed, PR #141: the island's doors drop after the island shuts, and a refused boot leaves no door answering. What stays owed rests in the porch (the rig's fixed settle window).
* `T33` ''A planted roll mark skips a roll'' (security, MEDIUM, predates `U1`; the train t2 cold read, wave three). `raisesMarkedAnswered` trusts any `rolled/<raise>` ledger row and `markRaiseRolled` stores no receipt; `ledger:edge` reads as synced (`operator-daemon-behavior.ts`) and the vessel-private class does not list it, so a planted mark makes seat-duties skip a removal roll and, beside `U1`'s durable owed list, clears that list. Cure: a mark counts only beside a kept roll whose receipt this vessel's key signed, and the ledger joins the vessel-private class. Red: plant a `rolled/<raise>` row from another device, remove a reader, and the roll still runs and the owed list keeps the raise; control: a vessel's own signed roll clears it. Landed, PR #144 (`13d24a218`): one row predicate shared by every reader and the writer counts a mark only under a receipt this vessel's own key signed, and `ledger:edge` crosses to no peer (vessel-private, a `device` owner no relation opens), classed for every face whose key the vessel holds at boot. What stays owed rests in the porch (faces whose keys open after boot).
* `T34` ''A joinee's own foundings never roll'' (security; the same read). A joinee runs no seat-duties, so a bag it founded never rolls its content key when a device leaves the fleet. Owed: the founding vessel rolls its own foundings on a counted removal, whatever its seat. Red: a joinee founds a bag, a device is removed, and a seal after the removal opens to no removed key; control: the seat holder's foundings roll as today. Landed, PR #144: the worn face decides the fleet, never the roster, so a joinee rolls its own foundings.
* `T35` ''A founder's first removal survives a restart unread'' (security, LOW-MEDIUM, consequence measured; the train t2 cold read, wave four, after `U1`'s `N1` cure). A founder's FIRST removal stays owed, the island restarts, and the fold reads unread (the worn fleet root null, or the root not served): the never-rolled gate passes and the removed device opens the post-restart seal. Cure: `fleetRaisesOf` answers `read:false` only for a vessel holding no root for the worn face (a joinee); a vessel with a roster but a null or unmatched worn fleet root throws, so the seal refuses. Red: that founder case refuses; control: a joinee with no roster seals. Probe: `~/.lares-scratch/cold-t2/probe/n1-cure.test.ts`. Takes the next free slot. Landed, PR #144: a worn face whose root or atom stands unread refuses to seal; only a vessel wearing no face reads unread.
* `T3` `LandedLedger.whenLanded`: an event replaces the wiki-shore 2 s poll. Red-first: a landing deferred past the old poll reds the poll form; a title that never lands times out with a named refusal. Clock stays injected. Files: `packages/lararium-tw5/src/landed-ledger.ts`, the `wiki-shore-*` tests. Landed, PR #142 (`86811edc5`): `LandedLedger.whenLanded` replaces the wiki-shore poll loops.
* `U1` The signer hand-over into the island with its chain check (the keystone, #/the-trains, O1). Built, PR #140 (`b333ed731`): a face's session seals into and reopens from the sealed store through a sign door, so no session key crosses into the island; only Nexus-anchored sessions seal, another face neither seals, opens nor reads, and the `sealed-*` verbs gate on the invocation's face; `holdsWrite` accepts only certificates under the vessel's own chain; a session act settles the bag's owed removal rolls before any seal, and the owed raises outlive a restart in the vessel's own fold. What stays owed rests in `U2` (the booking's nonce), and `K21` (sibling devices' seals). O1.
* ''The recovery-contact rename'' (#/rulings, 2026-10-31, recovery contacts, custodians and the Handle): built in PR #135. The `K18` recovery-key signer reads as a recovery contact across canon, code and the CLI, the seed-share holder as a custodian, and person-facing text says "your Handle" where recovery restores it; guardian keeps its human sense alone. What stays owed rests in `K18`. K.
* `L3` The MCP seat binds the hearth (walk gap G4). The seat's entry in the operator's home config named a deleted worktree copy of `lares_mcp.py` and carried no `LAR_ROOT`, and `~/.venv` held an `mcp` older than its pin, so the seat failed before it spoke. Landed, PR #148 (`1ef844c60`): `resolveLaresMcp(clone)` names the hearth's root (`LAR_ROOT`) in both the native and the surface-container forms and aims at the main clone, and every seat's observe compares env; the hearth owns its surface env (`<hearth>/lares-surface.env`), which the resolver and both container shims read, one layout with no fallback; a missing seat names its own form's cause; the seat's launch refuses by name on an `mcp` below its pin (2.3.0, welded to `requirements.txt` and the image lock); the e2e walk `mcp-seat-binds-the-hearth` reads `meme_put` with `recipe=default` and `lares meme get --recipe default` as the same bytes, and the e2e shards stand the holder venv. The operator's `~/.venv` took `mcp` 2.3.0 by hand (2026-11-01). Its tail, the operator's hand alone: `lares home tend` from the main clone re-writes the home entry, and a lane never runs it (#/cold-start). What stays owed rests in the porch (the holder venv's cache key, the checkout's `.env` under compose). L.
* `Q` ''The kupono grammar cut'' (#/rulings, 2026-11-01; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/grammar-watch#/the-kupono-cut`>>). Landed, PR #149 (`1e849cfba`), one lane merged once: every sigil value rides named in backticks; the bare arrow left the sigil, and the bearing pair `from=` and `to=` carries the relation; no `@` follows whitespace, and a phase glyph fuses onto its φ; the turn frame folds into one sigil, `set lares=` with `aim`, `steer` and `yield`, a steer carrying no `from`; the ward rides unprefixed; `wai` heads the wikispace conditional; `kahea` takes `name=`, `params=` and `mask=`. The boot seed reorganized through three blind cold readers and a Sonnet and Haiku dogfood wake, which spoke the new grammar every turn, and the operator approved its bytes, the turn frame provisionally. Readers and writers flipped; the plane names live in one constant; the turn harvesters burned whole (mesh turn and bearing harvest, the patch builder, the recall stamp filters, the tw5 bearing reader, the move skeleton, the self-read harvester, both VM harvesters, bare `lares sense pour <path>`, `form_encoder.py`, `loci_io.py`, `tools/turn-parity.mjs`); `docs/relational-parameter` burned by o-takiage, its parser trace now in `memetic-wikitext#/lexical-structure`; the `file-path` meta field retired (residency rides the envelope; 773 carriers stripped); the recall verb refuses a burned or search-only filter by name; `tools/grammar-cut.mjs` re-cuts all 790 carriers idempotent and never re-seals a broken seal; genesis re-baked once. The VSCode-TW5-Syntax pointer followed to its verified glass head (`0440b57dc`). What stays owed rests in `G47` (the three sensorium placeholders), `G48` (a rewound turn stays recallable), `G49` (recall arguments that drop unread), `G50` (a paired `wai` swallows its body), `G51` (`lar:` fragments inside tick values), the legacy-check pyre (#/side-lanes) and train ''R'' (#/the-trains). Q.

