!! The trains ~ each train's commits in order, what it waits on, and its riskiest step

''Rules every train keeps'': every commit leaves HEAD building, and a fix or batch boundary leaves its unit
suites green; red first, with a control, the red its own commit; `tools/typecheck-witness.sh` in every
battery; one e2e file locally and the whole sets on CI; one push per batch; a scratch root and a
scratch `HOME` for anything that writes custody. A step marked ''live'' changes a shape the
wire or a signature carries.

''The solo chain.'' Each of these holds the compose hunk in `open-node-vessel.ts` and
`open-browser-vessel.ts` while it runs, and no other node lane lands beside it: S, then K's seat, flip,
rename, scopes and founding act, then N's sealing and self-contracts, then W's three live steps, then W's
dials, then E, then O1's working address through its switch, then H's hosting act through its strangers' dial, then X.
T's stage-cut (`T12`) joins the chain as one named single-owner step after `T6`'s pins: for its window every other
lane stops at module boundaries.

!!! L ~ the memory-stage hearth (leads the road; waits on nothing above it; rows in #/stride-0-hearth)
# The walk's small rows: `L1`, `L2` and `L5` landed (PR #143), `L1` and `L2` keeping their tails; `L3` the MCP seat binds the hearth landed (PR #148), its tail the operator's `lares home tend`; then `L6` the seed's two of six and `L7` the wedged command.
# `F11`'s profile gate and Mask, before any agent writes the operator's own hearth.
# `L4`, the stage walk: a joined page's edit on disk, read back by the CLI and the MCP seat, and a CLI write shown in the page.
# The operator's hand: the fresh start on one machine, the founding, the unlock, the passphrase slot, the join acts, `lares home tend`.
# The stage: `L8`'s carrier first (its first commit carries canon), then `L9` to `L12` on the stage's own tools.
# `L13`, the move, the rung's acceptance; `L14`, the promotion verb, last; `L20`, the fiction and art domains, after the move.
''Gate'': ''Q'' landed (PR #149); ''R'' merges before `L4`, `L17` and `L8` to `L13` (#/the-order).
''Riskiest'': the join on the operator's own hearth, the first human-run walk of the full rites since the founding walk (PR #128); a wedge there costs a fresh start by hand, which the single-operator re-found ruling prices at nothing git cannot restore.

!!! R ~ block and inline sigils at TiddlyWiki's parsing parity (opens after ''Q''; merges before `L4`, `L17` and `L8` to `L13`; its plan rests in the controller's scratch, `train-r/plan-from-awakens.md`)
# The audit first: every reader that finds the seal by its place after ETX (attestation, the hearth's `ni:` readers, `carrier-check`, `stamp.mjs`).
# The spec and the frame law, red-first: the ETX foot carries its seal as a named `bcc` value beside `code` (the ETX slots already declare both), and the span check runs STX through ETX with the `bcc` slot blanked, DKIM-style, so the seal never hashes itself; a measure on the seed reads zero churn. The old trailer shape refuses for one commit, then burns.
# The frame code (`@lararium/memetic-frame`: the seal's reader, verifier and stamp, the postamble classifier, the span check), the fence mask and the generated grammar table.
# The corpus reshape and the seed: every foot line, and the one ahu closer that carries a hash suffix.
# The plugin rule and the readers: a block sigil counts only when its `>>` ends the line, and otherwise its paragraph holds an inline sigil, TiddlyWiki's own split; tree-sitter reads the same; text trailing a would-be block sigil reads as a recovered node with a diagnostic, never silent (the graceful floor). VSCode-TW5-Syntax's half rides Lares-Awakens' branch.
# The operator's two addons: every code fence in the boot seed names its grammar, and a seed law reds an unlabeled fence, the label strings agreed with Lares-Awakens first; a fence's tick run outruns the longest tick run inside it, a law over the seed and the whole corpus (the fork's codeblock already reads fences of any length).
''Gate'': security class (the frame shore), so a blind Opus read stands before the land; the seed's foot change takes the operator's look; its genesis bake and the deps lane's run one after the other.
''Riskiest'': the seal's move. A reader that finds the check by its place after ETX reads wrong until the audit names it, and a missed one fails a hearth's `ni:` read.

