''Launch kit'': <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/docs/train-o1-launch`>>.
# ''Landed ahead'': the session contract in mesh (`session-contract.ts`); the scoped document view (`session-document-view.ts`), the one recipe resolver's surface resolution (`surface-recipe.ts`, `resolveSurfaceRecipe`) and the pool's surface door (`mountSurface`), each specified in code and reached by no production caller. A builder reads P26's `peerArrivals` table and `protectedDocGuard` (PR #133) before touching the scoped view's seat.
# ''Built'' (PR #108, kit `docs/pono/hands-spine-lane`): the working document's address, node callers on sessions, the durability receipt, and the switch with the selector retired.
# The scoped document view's compose hunks: the per-surface facets in place of the face-fleet-view bridge (today's narrow share caller), the leaf's one-way gate and the hearth's twin.
# The recipe resolver's compose hunks: both platforms resolve at surface mount.
# The browser holder as owner.
# Browser surfaces and the control leg.
# The fleet view and removal.
''The keystone'' (the O1 read, 2026-10-31): the session signer stands, and its hand-over from a session's open into the daemon island's content-key holder stands too (`U1`), so the train runs as six feature units: `U1` the signer hand-over into the island with its chain check (landed, PR #140; #/o-takiage); then `U2` the node's surfaces under the scoped view, retiring the face-fleet-view bridge, whose facets never offer a live canon id since a session island bypasses the guard (`F1`); `U3` the fleet view and removal (`F10`) and `U4` the browser holder as owner (`F6` slice four, after `W4` and `B1`) beside `U2` on disjoint files; then `U5` sealed-store step 3; then `U6` per-face content-key seats (`K21`). `U1`'s tail rides `U2`: a session booking keys on a nonce main mints for session-placed invocations, never the computable face-scoped id; the island's verifier gains a `dispose`, so a suite's islands unsubscribe their seat rolls; and "answered" holds per raise, not per bag, latent until the grant ring reads by face key.
''Riskiest'': the working address, where an attach that cannot stand refuses the boot.

!!! H ~ the hosted road's re-cut (its pure introduction landed; the rest waits on K's founding act and W's cutover, and lands whole before X)
''Launch kit'': <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/docs/train-h-launch`>>.
# ''Landed ahead'': the introduction, pure (`introduction.ts`); H2's delegation and three dials (`hosting-delegation.ts`); H8's signed grant and public-half verifier (`walker-grant.ts`).
# ''Live'': the issuer, reader, hosting store and sorter take the one hosting-act cut; the serving rows receive grant public halves before E's walker arm.
