!! Side lanes ~ queued beside the road, each on its own files

* ''The shadow at the gates.'' The law of removal's reach stands whole at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/reach`>> (operator ruling): four marked edges, two hands, rolls that carry shadows, a ledger that keeps what a reader counted, a consult at every gate, and keys that never outrun standing. <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/what-the-code-holds`>> names each part the code holds and each part that stays owed, and this carrier keeps no copy of that list. The cosign door's verdicts and envelope stand ready for train N's door to adopt. The sealed store's key roll subscribes to the seat's roll and lands with its own train.
* ''Handle resolver wiring and cross-log order.'' A Handle reader that holds no owner-head resolver trusts the inception alone. Owed: the resolver's wiring, where it must answer "the current, unsuperseded, un-vetoed head" and never "a key that once stood as head", and the order between a Handle's log and its owner's log.
* ''The clock cures.'' The audit of each remaining contract, Cabal and Handle door runs relation by relation, never as a blind sweep (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/causal-island#/selected-contracts`>>).
* ''The mirror and custody arc'' (train D, <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap`>>), each its own whole capability in this order: `M2` the camera under `$tw.rootWidget` with root services read through a capability, and the route door; `M3` the CSP crossing fence before the CAS read, the violation alert and the http-request door seam; `M4` the full-against-stock goldens, the WebKit golden and the phone probe; `K2` custody and signers in the worker; `K3` the clean-realm ceremony with passphrase and passkey on equal footing; `S` the browser store's sealed-rest steps 2 and 3, after which `sealedRest` reaches the mirror's boot inputs and the plugin gate opens for sealed vessels; `D4` the Wiki Actor.
* ''The code lane.'' False source comments (`G6` of #/after-the-seat); callers that still mount a layer default-writable (`operator-daemon-behavior.ts`, `daemon-vm-core.ts`); mesh tests that sit outside the type-check.
* ''The Harbor tail'': train A.
* ''Early starts beside the chain'': the node, CLI and tool fixtures funnel of train K.
* ''Band-ladder residue'': one five-band ladder, the `lar_feedback` output field name. It rides the Sensorium's wait, and a frame inside it may heal at any time.
* ''The capture lane's era ruling'': #/open.
* ''The seed seat's open research'': the hosts it seats stand measured; scout quality, compaction, the linkless checkout, VS Code, Copilot's cloud surfaces and the seats outside the clone stand open (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/seed-seat#/the-research`>>).
* ''The reality tunnel's memory shore'': the ingest rows (Claude's Stop and SessionEnd, Codex's Stop, Copilot's sessionEnd) hold while the mempalace stands absent, and `tend` lifts an ingest hook already present, the gate derived from the memory shore the way the MCP seats read theirs; until it lands, `lares hooks pause` holds them, since the sensorium rests until the founded-Lararium proof (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/cli/reality-tunnel`>>). Once the memory stage stands (`L13`), the same shore decides whether a harness's own memory reads from the stage.
* ''The operator's declarations win'' (design unfinished): an operator's own choice outranks the tunnel on every home row it names, so `tend` never overrides it. The rows that override today: retention (Codex's `history.persistence` and Copilot's `commandHistoryMaxSize` set whole, Claude's floor raising a lower `cleanupPeriodDays`), the `lares` bin link re-aiming a link the operator set on purpose, a prose line carrying the seed's link lifted whole, and a file left holding frontmatter alone deleted. Open: where a declaration rests (a home-side file the tunnel reads, or a mark per row) and how `verify` reads a row the operator holds (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/cli/reality-tunnel`>>).
* ''The CLI's test laws'': the pattern-integrity precedent train T builds on (#/stride-t-recut, `T18`); the lares CLI's suite re-cut as sixteen laws over the live tables, its literal bug-finds kept as seeds and its strength read by named mutants; every law stands built for at least one domain, and the doors each law has yet to reach stand named in its row (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/cli-test-laws#/the-laws`>>).
* ''DreamDOM, train D'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-16: DreamDOM names the superset of cameras, every root template over every document sink across the one engine per wiki). The model stands whole in <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom`>>; its phases `D0` to `D7` and rows `D1` to `D17` read in <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap`>>, and this carrier keeps no copy of them. `F8`'s control-event leg rides the roadmap's camera-contract phase.
* ''Sealed-store step 3'': sealed Repo storage values, hydration checked against the session's face, and the fresh base a from-now admission needs. A face's own names ride its persona plane only once that plane's rest seals, so `lares persona sync` carries nothing until this step lands. The production session signer exists (dials and the CLI door mint one), and its hand-over into the daemon island with the chain check stands (`U1`, PR #140). It also waits on ONE FACE (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/sealed-store#/owed`>>).
* ''The face-key roll'': a paper restore's successor, owed in `face-proof.mem` (line 213), the roll that follows a restore from paper.
* ''The whole-record conflict resolution verb'': split from `P26`, whose Kahu-reach and steward-succession parts landed; the verb that resolves a whole record in conflict stays owed.
* ''`I3`'s S2 cross-device fence'': a signed claim checked at the sink; the ruling stands pending with the operator.
* ''A two-face e2e with an aliased wiki'': `ralias`'s island step stays source-backed until a two-face e2e carries an aliased wiki.
* ''A CI cells and shards rebalance, its tail'': `ci-ten` (PR #145) fits a full run into ten concurrent jobs (13 with the fail-closed gates), deals the node suite by measured file weight under a union law and raises one run per lane push. Owed: the held-out 24 cells shrink to about 8; e2e shard 1's hook cost joins its weights, the long pole that holds the critical path near 22 minutes where about 16 stands reachable.
* ''The local merge queue's tail'' (`land-queue`, PR #146): its two re-reads named LOWs: the held-out gate skips speculative trains, path-only classing misses imports and submodule bumps, the lock and enqueue races, a crash between the span push and the entry's settle misreports, and `--local` lands with no cloud read on one flag.
* ''The deps before the founding'' (#/the-order, rank 1c; #/rulings, 2026-11-01; the dep survey rests in the controller's scratch, `dep-survey/report.md`). One lane after ''Q'', since the lockfile moves, its two engine leans decided by trials. `@automerge/automerge` moves 3.4.1 to 3.5.0 if Trial A reads green: the whole suite and every e2e set on 3.5.0, beside a grep for `__proto__`-keyed documents, which 3.5.0 refuses; the hold's old ground, stored fragments, never applies to a house that stores none. The trials read on 2026-11-01: Trial A GREEN (every suite equal to its control, every e2e set green, no `__proto__`-keyed doc, genesis unmoved), so `@automerge/automerge` moves to 3.5.0; Trial B RED, so `@keyhive/keyhive` holds 0.3.0-alpha.1 through the founding: 0.6.0 stands from its Archive yet inverts four house laws (revocation authority, the forward-only boundary, the event-only stand, a revocation naming its subject), and its port waits past the founding (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/keyhive-zero-six-port`>>). `vitest` and its browser packages move to 5.0.5, which cures the dev-server advisory, and the hygiene bumps the survey ranks ride along (`ws`, `smol-toml`, `vite`, `esbuild`, the `web-tree-sitter` and `tree-sitter-cli` pair together, `playwright` with its image tag, `@types/node`, `acorn`, pnpm inside 11). Subduction and Onomancy stay out, their wall-clock grounds measured unchanged, and TiddlyWiki stays an epoch act. Automerge and esbuild bind the engine bytes, so the lane re-bakes genesis once, after ''R''s bake, never beside it; a Keyhive move re-reads `W11`'s four alarms.
* ''The legacy-check pyre'' (#/the-order, rank 1d; #/rulings, 2026-11-01; its plan rests in the controller's scratch, `legacy-pyre/plan.md`). Gated: it opens once the house stands and the MCP seat answers (the operator's founding and `lares home tend`), after ''R'' and the deps lane land. A Sonnet cold reader sorts every check across every era, in code, tests, witnesses, frozen fixtures and canon prose, seeded by ''Q''s keep-and-burn ledger: KEEP where it guards a live invariant and would catch a fresh mistake, BURN where it refuses only a spelling the tree no longer holds or blocks a person's legit choice, SPLIT where one part does each. Its known positive comes first: the `file-path` deny in the deserializer, its `meme check` red and its witness leg. A blind Opus security reader then reads each BURN row with planted inputs on a scratch root, since a refusal of an old form can double as an injection or smuggling guard, and answers burn-safe, burn-with-replacement (naming the live invariant that replaces it) or keep-for-security. One lane then burns, red-first where a burn changes behaviour, under the whole witness fleet and full CI, as security class.
* ''The `shore-writes` dropdown flake'': three sightings so far; it wants a CI failure artifact before a cure.
* ''The porch'', a standing hygiene lane beside the slots, each row red-first with its control:
** ''The genesis pin's crash window'' (`L5`'s tail): `pinGenesisSeed` removes and rewrites the pin with a plain write, never atomically (route it through `publishFile`); a crash between a founding's success and the pin write leaves a fresh vessel unpinned, and a non-force `found` skips without healing it (write the pin on the skipped path where none stands and the seed resolves shipped); the tests cover only the pre-custody refusal.
** ''The intent relay's cell order'' (`T19`'s tail, owned by `T6`'s boot pins): nothing behaviour-tests that the composer puts `intentRelayService` in its cell before the first sweep (`open-node-vessel.ts`), and the wired census passes a reverted order.
** ''A found over a standing home names the state'': `lares vessel found` over a standing custody home with no place key refuses "no key file ... run lares vessel found", advice that loops; the refusal names the state (a home stands without a place key: move it aside or restore it), never an old name.
** ''The persona-root matcher'': the pattern no longer matches a leading-zero index (`-h01`); confirm no writer emits one, else widen the matcher.
** ''A silent-zero instrument'': `node tools/two-phase-boot.test.mjs` run directly exits 0 on a failure (a bare `process.exit()` in its `finally`); `node --test`, the CI glob, reports it.
** ''A runaway inside one file'' (VSCode-TW5-Syntax `tools/composition-check.js`, Lares-Awakens' side): the check misses a runaway that starts inside one file, so the seed read zero failures while broken (2026-11-01); a planted single-file runaway reds it first.
** ''The holder venv's cache key'' (`L3`'s tail): `ci.yml` and `e2e-shards.yml` key the cached `~/.venv` on `mempalace/pyproject.toml` and the sensorium requirements alone, so a mempalace submodule commit or a Python patch release reuses a stale venv; the key takes the submodule's commit and the interpreter's full version.
** ''The checkout's `.env` under compose'' (`L3`'s tail): with no hearth env file and the mounts named in the shell, compose still auto-loads the checkout's `.env`, a second layout the one-layout law refuses; the shims hand compose the hearth's env file or none.
** ''The veil reader'': `packages/lararium-sensorium/scripts/worldline_veil.py` expects a persona root in the clear at the identity root, while roots now rest encrypted per face, so it reads nothing; a sensorium porch item.
** ''The carried-Nexus rig's notes'' (`T19`'s and `T27`'s tails): `T19`'s `chmod 000` case bites nothing under root (a false red alone); `seatStranger` leaks its dial when the seat fails; `T27`'s rig waits a fixed 3 s settle window.
** ''Faces whose keys open after boot'' (`T33`'s tail): a face the vessel holds but does not wear gets its ledger classed vessel-private only when it mounts, so its frontier pins and seen rows stay reachable through a realm alias until then (its marks still need receipts); the cure reads atom keys before custody opens.

