<<~ ahu slot=`#/open`>>

!! Open ~ what the operator owns

!!! Seats, custody and recovery
# ''Recovery contacts and recovery.'' The enrolment shape stands ruled (#/rulings). Request authentication, the veto, a person's death and succession, the catastrophe rite and any third key, and a Handle's DNS binding stand open at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu#/seed-and-nexus`>>.
# ''A sealed receipt manifest for carriage.'' It would let a root restored from paper re-open its carriage after device loss — and would turn carriage toward the backup W rules it never becomes. The lenses split; re-opening W needs the operator's turned key.
# ''Carriage across leaves.'' A guest-held carry-claim proven at the carry door would let carriage follow a guest across leaves — a second relation and a second domain. Lean: not built.
# ''The reading of "delegated keys" for cloud carriers'', deferred until the operator can deploy to a cloud surface (#/the-road).
# ''House leans the operator may overturn'': the floor vessel key drops its next-key commitment; the long-silent device rule; the strangers' dial drops the newest arrival (#/decisions); the seal's standing leans (`S7` of #/stride-1-spine).

!!! Planes and offerings
# ''The offering's `offer` and `witness` caps'' against the Lamplighter stack.
# ''The crossing record.'' Its durable emission threshold (lean: authority, vessel, federation and externally meaningful-effect boundaries alone), and whether a destination receipt always signs separately (lean: yes).
# ''Engine cadence'': who holds a cadence share and the epoch pin stand ruled (#/rulings); whether partial conformance lands before `kahuli engine` un-holds (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu#/contract`>>).
# ''Grammar submissions'': whether the Nexus Kahu or the corpus-kahu receive them.
# ''DNS custody past the credential'': delegated `_acme-challenge`, record custody, the ACME account and CAA travel as one question (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/bounded-reach-contract`>>). With it: whether a host timer or a hand runs renewal, and the answer for a phone that forces encrypted DNS.
# ''The crossroads mirror's filter'' (`G21` of #/operator-gates).
# ''Removal's reach.'' The model stands ruled (#/rulings; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/four-edges`>>). Five questions stay the operator's, each with the house's lean. Whether an edge act may ever use the emergency class (lean: never). Whether a seated member under a member shadow keeps a seat's signature until the next roll (lean: yes, a seat leaves by a roll alone). What a recovery council holds after a mutual removal (lean: nothing built; the fork stands as the one exit). Whether a holder's key reads at its log's current head, so a recovered face keeps its edges (lean: yes, owed with the resolver of #/side-lanes). Whether a counted raise moves the keys while a lift still races it (lean: yes, remove-wins reaches the keys, and a lift then seats afresh). Two more came with the key side. What removes a seat no standing hand can revoke, the founding vessel's own among them (lean: a fresh group, at the re-founding that moves the PersonaGroup to a Keyhive group). Whether a vessel that holds no revoke authority goes on trying a raise until it sees the seat leave (lean: yes, and each try hands the roll on again, so the content key rolls whoever revokes the seat).
# ''The self-slot inner ring.'' Wiring it freezes a naming: a bag URL through a live ring hashes to seed its document, and a re-name costs a re-founding. Lean: widen the bridge first, and wire the ring on an explicit ruling alone.

!!! Shore, grammar and code
# ''The ungated slot child.'' A slot child's native save never grades; three child-edit shapes stand marked as the operator's call (`packages/lararium-tw5/tests/meme-backstop.test.ts`; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/syncer-back-parity`>>).
# ''Ruling-gated mesh modules'' (listed in the header of `packages/lararium-mesh/src/index.ts`): `recipe`, `readiness`, `reaction-graph`, `pronaos`, `offering-inspection`. Each moves or stays by ruling alone.
# ''The capture cell'' sits apart for review in `packages/lararium-mesh/src/capture/`, `packages/lararium-node/src/capture/`, `packages/lararium-tw5/src/capture/` and `packages/lares-cli/src/commands/capture/`. Canon places capture in Python per stream with the TS daemon coordinating alone (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/capture-annotation-model`>>), while the TS cell carries the live path. Rule: retire it to Python, or re-home it.
# ''Receipt names and verb capabilities.'' Whether a receipt's address follows the house's own kind nouns or the content-addressed surface; and the table that maps each routed verb to its capability, where `deriveRoutedCap` answers for every routed verb today (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/verb-local-dispatch.ts`).
# ''Rulings that rest in their own carriers'': the promotion receipt's fields (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/canon-boundary`>>), the one-of-one mantle (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/handle-card`>>), the lease's questions (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/realm-bag-brief`>>), and the offering's questions (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/heraldry`>>).
# ''Two Kairoses.'' The fiction names KAIROS as a watcher that speaks unasked; the code's Kairos pet-names an unbuilt entity that refreshes an OAuth grant at the right moment (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/reach-plane`>>). One entity, or two that share a name?
# ''Alerts and shadows.'' Whether a disk conflict that arrives while no wiki stands pinned raises its alert at the next pin; whether a hand that deletes its override of a shadow leaves a delete, where today the shadow's text gets saved as a record; whether the page warns when a browser has joined no face.
# ''The confirm door upstream.'' The fork asks its questions through the wiki itself (`$tw.utils.confirm`, `tm-confirm`). Owed before a donation: the order of actions after a confirm, a switch for a blocking prompt, and one squashed change. The withdrawn render boundary's upstream pull request, if it still stands open, advertises a design the fork backed out.
# ''The realm consult's root map'' (`peerContractNymMap`, `open-node-vessel.ts`): a seat held by <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/membership-doctrine#/two-maps`>> and the house ruling of 2026-10-16 (#/rulings, a realm's steward map holds leaves), filled only by a root edge proven at the seat. Nothing fills it today and its readers fail closed. The house leans keep it and name an owed row for its filler (`T29` states its law).
# ''The barrel re-exported names'' (487): they wait on their own ruling before `T4`'s sweep reaches them.
# ''One sentence for the `CLAUDE.md` adapter note'', the operator's to place: the CLI's ingest, watch and REPACK derive against `LAR_BAGS` and `LAR_WIKIS`, so "read neither" holds for the daemon's projection mirrors alone.

